  'Option A (correct) is Amazon EventBridge. It can receive events from various AWS services, including Amazon S3, and route them to targets like AWS Lambda functions. Option B, AWS Systems Manager Automation, is for executing operational runbooks, not primarily for event routing. Option C, Amazon CloudWatch Logs, collects and monitors logs, but doesn''t directly trigger actions based on S3 events. Option D, AWS Config, tracks resource configuration changes for compliance, not for real-time event-driven compute.',
