INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_22_m_22_2_83',
  'A critical application running on Amazon EC2 instances occasionally experiences system-level failures that render instances unreachable, requiring manual intervention to restore service. The SysOps team wants to implement a solution that automatically detects these failures and recovers the affected instances to a healthy state with MINIMAL downtime and manual effort. Which solution meets this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure EC2 Auto Recovery for the instances and enable a CloudWatch alarm on System Status Check failures.","Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to trigger an AWS Lambda function that stops and starts the instance upon failure.","Implement an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that is manually executed when an instance becomes unreachable.","Rely on Amazon CloudWatch default metrics to detect failures and manually replace the instances."]'::json,
  '{0}'::int[],
  'Option A (correct) is the most effective and automated solution. Configuring EC2 Auto Recovery for an instance, combined with a CloudWatch alarm on System Status Check failures, will automatically recover the instance on a new healthy host while preserving its original attributes (instance ID, private IP, EIP). This significantly minimizes downtime and manual intervention (anti-pattern ap-1.2-001). Option B (incorrect) would involve more complex setup and management of Lambda functions and might not preserve all instance attributes. Option C (incorrect) requires manual execution, which contradicts the goal of minimal manual effort. Option D (incorrect) requires manual replacement and doesn''t provide automatic recovery, leading to significant downtime.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_22_m_22_2_84',
  'A company operates a critical application that relies on multiple AWS services. They need to ensure proactive awareness of potential service disruptions or scheduled maintenance events that could impact their specific account and resources, rather than just relying on the public AWS Service Health Dashboard. Which approach ensures they receive personalized notifications?',
  'mcq',
  '["Subscribe to the public AWS Service Health Dashboard RSS feed.","Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms on application-specific metrics.","Regularly review AWS CloudTrail logs for service-related API errors.","Subscribe to AWS Health events via Amazon EventBridge and send notifications to an Amazon SNS topic."]'::json,
  '{3}'::int[],
  'Option D (correct) is the best approach to receive personalized, proactive notifications. AWS Health provides account-specific information about AWS service health events. By integrating AWS Health events with Amazon EventBridge, you can create rules to capture these specific events and route them to an Amazon SNS topic for notifications (e.g., email, SMS), ensuring proactive awareness (anti-pattern ap-1.2-002). Option A (incorrect) provides generic service status, not account-specific impacts. Option B (incorrect) monitors application metrics, not AWS service health events. Option C (incorrect) audits API calls, which is reactive and not designed for proactive service health notifications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_22_m_22_2_85',
  'A SysOps Administrator has configured an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to detect high CPU utilization on an Amazon EC2 instance. When this alarm enters an ''ALARM'' state, the administrator wants to automatically trigger an action to scale out the application by adding another EC2 instance. Which AWS service should be used to initiate this automated response?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail to log the alarm state change.","Amazon EventBridge to route the alarm state change event to an Auto Scaling policy.","AWS Systems Manager Automation to manually execute a runbook.","AWS Trusted Advisor to recommend scaling actions."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the appropriate service. Amazon EventBridge can be configured with a rule to detect specific CloudWatch alarm state changes (e.g., from OK to ALARM). This rule can then be set to trigger an Auto Scaling policy to scale out the application, automating the response to high CPU utilization. Option A (incorrect) logs API activity, it does not trigger automated actions. Option C (incorrect) is for automating operational tasks, but for a direct response to a CloudWatch alarm, EventBridge is the more direct and event-driven mechanism to integrate with Auto Scaling. Option D (incorrect) provides recommendations, not automated actions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_22_m_22_2_86',
  'A SysOps Administrator is tasked with proactively identifying opportunities to reduce AWS spending, improve system performance, and enhance security posture across their organization''s AWS accounts. Which AWS service provides actionable recommendations based on an analysis of their AWS environment against best practices?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Trusted Advisor","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config","AWS Health Dashboard"]'::json,
  '{0}'::int[],
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Trusted Advisor. It is a service that provides recommendations to help you follow AWS best practices. These recommendations cover five categories: cost optimization, performance, security, fault tolerance, and service limits, making it ideal for proactively identifying areas for improvement and cost reduction. Option B (incorrect) is a monitoring service for metrics and logs. Option C (incorrect) tracks resource configuration changes and compliance. Option D (incorrect) provides personalized information about AWS service health events, not general best practice recommendations for your account.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

