  'Option B (The maximum acceptable amount of data loss after an incident) correctly defines the Recovery Point Objective (RPO). It specifies the point in time to which data must be recovered. Option A is about cost, not RPO. Option C (The maximum acceptable downtime after an incident) defines the Recovery Time Objective (RTO). Option D also describes RTO.',
