  'Option A (AWS Application Auto Scaling) is the correct service. It enables you to automatically scale scalable resources for services beyond Amazon EC2, such as Amazon DynamoDB tables, Amazon ECS services, and Amazon Aurora Replicas. Option B (Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling) is specifically for EC2 instances. Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is an infrastructure as code service. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) helps manage your AWS resources but is not an auto-scaling service.',
