  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (On-Demand capacity mode) offers the LEAST operational overhead for a DynamoDB table with highly variable traffic. It automatically adjusts capacity based on actual usage, eliminating the need for manual provisioning or auto scaling configuration. Option A (Provisioned capacity mode with manual adjustments) requires constant monitoring and manual intervention. Option B (Provisioned capacity mode with auto scaling) reduces overhead compared to manual, but still requires configuration and monitoring of scaling policies. Option D (Reserved capacity mode) is a pricing model for long-term savings, not a capacity management mode.',
