  '["Simple scaling policy, which triggers on a single alarm threshold.","Step scaling policy, which adjusts capacity in steps based on alarm breaches.","Scheduled scaling policy, for predictable traffic patterns.","Target Tracking scaling policy, which maintains a desired metric average."]'::json,
  '{3}'::int[],
  'Option D (Target Tracking scaling policy, which maintains a desired metric average) is the most suitable policy type for maintaining CPU utilization around a specific target (e.g., 60%). It automatically adjusts the Auto Scaling group''s capacity to keep the metric as close as possible to the target value. Option A (Simple scaling policy) and Option B (Step scaling policy) are less dynamic and require more manual tuning to achieve a specific average. Option C (Scheduled scaling policy) is for predictable, time-based scaling, not reactive scaling based on metrics.',
