INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_51',
  'Which AWS Systems Manager capability allows you to remotely and securely execute commands on one or more Amazon EC2 instances or on-premises servers?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Session Manager","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Run Command. It allows you to remotely and securely manage the configuration of your instances, executing commands like shell scripts, PowerShell commands, or AWS-provided documents on one or more instances. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Session Manager) provides interactive shell access to instances. Option B (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) is for defining and maintaining a consistent configuration across instances. Option D (AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager) automates the patching process for operating systems and applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_52',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to securely access an Amazon EC2 instance without opening inbound SSH ports or managing SSH keys. Which AWS Systems Manager capability should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS Systems Manager Session Manager","AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager","AWS Systems Manager State Manager"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Session Manager. It provides secure and auditable instance management without the need to open inbound ports, manage SSH keys, or use bastion hosts. It supports interactive one-click browser-based or CLI access. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Run Command) is for executing commands but doesn''t provide interactive shell access without open ports in the same way Session Manager does. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager) automates patching. Option D (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) ensures instances comply with desired configurations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_53',
  'Which AWS Systems Manager capability automates the process of scanning instances for missing patches and applying them, helping to maintain security compliance?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager","AWS Systems Manager Session Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager. It automates the process of patching managed instances with security updates and other types of updates. It can scan instances for missing patches and apply them according to a defined schedule. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Run Command) executes commands but doesn''t specifically automate patching. Option B (AWS Systems Manager State Manager) maintains a consistent configuration, which can include patch baselines, but Patch Manager is the dedicated service for patch automation. Option D (AWS Systems Manager Session Manager) provides secure interactive access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_54',
  'Which AWS service is best suited for automating operational tasks in response to events, such as processing data after an S3 object is uploaded or stopping EC2 instances on a schedule, with minimal server management?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Lambda. It is a serverless compute service that lets you run code without provisioning or managing servers. It''s ideal for event-driven operational automation, such as responding to S3 events, scheduled events (via Amazon EventBridge), or API calls. Option A (Amazon EC2) involves managing virtual servers, which is not minimal server management. Option C (AWS CodeDeploy) automates application deployments, not general operational tasks in response to events. Option D (AWS OpsWorks) is a configuration management service for automating server configuration and application deployment, which involves managing servers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_55',
  'A company needs to automate the deployment of application code to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. Which AWS service is specifically designed for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS Lambda","AWS CodeDeploy","Amazon EventBridge"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS CodeDeploy. It automates code deployments to Amazon EC2 instances, AWS Fargate, AWS Lambda, and on-premises servers. It handles the complexity of updating applications and minimizes downtime during deployment. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Run Command) can execute commands on instances but is not a full-fledged application deployment service with rollback capabilities. Option B (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service for running code in response to events, not for deploying applications to EC2 fleets. Option D (Amazon EventBridge) is a serverless event bus that makes it easier to connect applications together, but it does not deploy application code itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_56',
  'A SysOps team wants to provide secure, audited remote access to Amazon EC2 instances for troubleshooting without requiring open inbound ports or managing SSH keys. Which solution BEST meets this requirement and adheres to AWS best practices?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure a bastion host with SSH access in a public subnet.","Utilize AWS Systems Manager Session Manager.","Enable RDP access directly to instances from specific IP ranges.","Deploy AWS OpsWorks to manage instance configurations and access."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is to utilize AWS Systems Manager Session Manager. Session Manager provides secure, audited, and browser-based or CLI-based interactive shell access to EC2 instances without requiring open inbound ports (like SSH or RDP) or managing SSH keys, aligning with AWS best practices for secure access. Option A (Configure a bastion host with SSH access in a public subnet) requires managing SSH keys and still involves open inbound ports to the bastion host, which is less secure than Session Manager. Option C (Enable RDP access directly to instances from specific IP ranges) requires opening inbound RDP ports and managing credentials, which is less secure and has higher operational overhead than Session Manager. Option D (Deploy AWS OpsWorks to manage instance configurations and access) is a configuration management service that does not primarily provide secure, interactive remote access without open ports.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_57',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to ensure all Amazon EC2 instances in a fleet are consistently patched with the latest security updates without manual intervention. Which AWS service should be configured to automate this process?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager","AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager. It is specifically designed to automate the process of scanning instances for missing patches and applying them according to a defined schedule and patch baseline, ensuring consistent security updates without manual intervention. Option B (AWS Systems Manager Run Command) can execute patch commands, but Patch Manager provides the full automation, scanning, and compliance reporting. Option C (AWS CodeDeploy) is for application deployment, not OS patching. Option D (AWS Lambda) can be used for custom automation, but Patch Manager is the purpose-built service for OS patching, offering a more integrated and lower-overhead solution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_58',
  'Which AWS Systems Manager capability helps define and maintain a consistent configuration for your Amazon EC2 instances, ensuring they comply with specific policies over time?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Run Command","AWS Systems Manager State Manager","AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager","AWS Systems Manager Session Manager"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Systems Manager State Manager. It helps you define and maintain a consistent configuration for your Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers. You can use State Manager to apply configuration settings, enforce patch compliance, or bootstrap software, ensuring instances remain in a desired state. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Run Command) is for executing commands on demand. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager) focuses specifically on patching. Option D (AWS Systems Manager Session Manager) provides secure interactive access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_59',
  'Which AWS service is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together, routing events from AWS services, SaaS applications, and your own applications to various targets for processing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon EventBridge. It is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together by routing events from various sources (AWS services, SaaS applications, custom applications) to targets like AWS Lambda, Amazon SNS, or Amazon SQS for processing. Option A (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service. Option B (Amazon SNS) is a pub/sub messaging service. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service that can be a target for EventBridge events, but EventBridge itself is the event bus.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain24_5',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_24_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

