  'Option A (correct) accurately describes the primary purpose of AWS Systems Manager Session Manager. It enables secure, browser-based or CLI-based shell access to EC2 instances without requiring open inbound ports, bastion hosts, or managing SSH keys, enhancing security and auditability. Option B describes AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager. Option C describes AWS CodeDeploy. Option D describes AWS CloudFormation.',
