VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_64',
  'A SysOps team needs to securely access EC2 instances for troubleshooting without opening inbound SSH ports or managing SSH keys. They also require session activity to be logged for auditing purposes. Which service provides this capability with the LEAST operational overhead?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure an EC2 instance as a bastion host and use SSH through it.","Use AWS Systems Manager Session Manager to connect to the instances.","Enable RDP access for Windows instances and manage credentials manually.","Implement a VPN connection to the VPC and then use direct SSH."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Session Manager, which provides secure, audited shell access to EC2 instances without requiring open inbound ports or managing SSH keys, directly addressing the requirements with minimal operational overhead and logging capabilities. Option A, using a bastion host, requires managing an additional EC2 instance, its security, and SSH keys, increasing operational overhead (anti-pattern ap-3.2-001). Option C, enabling RDP, requires open inbound ports and manual credential management, which is less secure and higher overhead (anti-pattern ap-3.2-001). Option D, implementing a VPN, adds significant network configuration and management overhead, which is not the least operational overhead.',
