VALUES (
  'q_24_m_24_2_68',
  'A SysOps team needs to automatically stop all non-production Amazon EC2 instances outside business hours (e.g., every weekday at 7 PM) to save costs. Which AWS service combination provides the MOST automated and serverless solution?',
  'mcq',
  '["Manually stop instances using the AWS Management Console daily.","Use an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to trigger an AWS Lambda function.","Create an AWS Systems Manager Run Command document to stop instances and execute it manually.","Develop a custom script on an EC2 instance to call the EC2 StopInstances API."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) provides the most automated and serverless solution. An Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule can trigger an AWS Lambda function at a specified time, and the Lambda function can then use the AWS SDK to stop the desired EC2 instances. This approach requires no servers to manage for the automation itself. Option A is a manual process and does not meet the automation requirement. Option C requires manual execution of the Run Command document, which is not fully automated. Option D requires running and managing an EC2 instance solely for automation, which is not serverless and adds operational overhead.',
