INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_36',
  'A SysOps Administrator is configuring a new Amazon VPC. Which component is responsible for allowing outbound internet access for instances in a private subnet while preventing inbound internet access?',
  'mcq',
  '["Internet Gateway","VPC Endpoint","NAT Gateway","VPC Peering Connection"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the NAT Gateway. A NAT Gateway allows instances in a private subnet to connect to services outside your VPC (e.g., the internet) but prevents external services from initiating connections to those instances. Option A (incorrect) An Internet Gateway allows direct bidirectional internet access for instances in a public subnet. Option B (incorrect) A VPC Endpoint allows private connectivity to AWS services without traversing the internet. Option D (incorrect) A VPC Peering Connection connects two VPCs, enabling communication between them, but does not provide internet access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_37',
  'Which AWS service enables you to create a private connection between your on-premises data center and your Amazon VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Peering","AWS Direct Connect","AWS Transit Gateway","VPC Endpoints"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Direct Connect, which establishes a dedicated network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS, providing a consistent and high-bandwidth private connection. Option A (incorrect) VPC Peering connects two VPCs, enabling communication between them, but it is not for connecting to on-premises data centers. Option C (incorrect) AWS Transit Gateway connects VPCs and on-premises networks through a central hub, but it still requires a VPN or Direct Connect for the on-premises connection itself. Option D (incorrect) VPC Endpoints allow private access to AWS services from within your VPC, not from on-premises networks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_38',
  'What is the primary function of a Network Access Control List (NACL) in an Amazon VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["To control inbound and outbound traffic for an EC2 instance.","To control inbound and outbound traffic for a subnet.","To manage routing between subnets.","To provide a firewall for web applications."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the primary function of a Network Access Control List (NACL). NACLs act as a stateless firewall for controlling traffic in and out of one or more subnets. Option A (incorrect) describes a Security Group, which acts as a stateful firewall for EC2 instances. Option C (incorrect) managing routing between subnets is the function of route tables. Option D (incorrect) providing a firewall for web applications is typically handled by AWS WAF, not NACLs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_39',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to connect multiple Amazon VPCs to a shared on-premises network and also enable communication between these VPCs in a hub-and-spoke topology. Which AWS networking service is designed for this scalable inter-VPC and hybrid connectivity?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Peering connections between all VPCs.","AWS Direct Connect for each VPC to on-premises.","AWS Transit Gateway.","VPC Endpoints for each VPC."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Transit Gateway. It acts as a network transit hub, connecting VPCs and on-premises networks through a central point, simplifying network management and providing a scalable hub-and-spoke model. Option A (incorrect) represents anti-pattern ap-5.1-001. Using VPC Peering for hub-and-spoke connectivity between many VPCs is not scalable because VPC peering connections are non-transitive and require N*(N-1)/2 connections for full mesh, leading to complex management. Option B (incorrect) AWS Direct Connect for each VPC to on-premises would be costly and operationally complex for multiple VPCs, as Transit Gateway can centralize the on-premises connection. Option D (incorrect) VPC Endpoints provide private connectivity to AWS services, not inter-VPC or hybrid network connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_40',
  'Which AWS service provides private connectivity from your Amazon VPC to AWS services without using an Internet Gateway, NAT Gateway, VPN connection, or AWS Direct Connect connection?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Peering","AWS Transit Gateway","VPC Endpoints (AWS PrivateLink)","AWS Site-to-Site VPN"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is VPC Endpoints, specifically Interface Endpoints powered by AWS PrivateLink. These allow you to privately connect your VPC to supported AWS services and VPC endpoint services powered by PrivateLink without requiring an Internet Gateway, NAT Gateway, VPN, or Direct Connect. Option A (incorrect) VPC Peering connects two VPCs, not a VPC to AWS services privately. Option B (incorrect) AWS Transit Gateway connects VPCs and on-premises networks, but not directly to AWS services in a private manner like VPC Endpoints. Option D (incorrect) AWS Site-to-Site VPN provides a secure connection between your VPC and your on-premises network over the internet, which is not what is requested for private AWS service access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_41',
  'What is the purpose of an Elastic IP address in Amazon EC2?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a dynamic public IP address that changes upon instance restart.","To provide a static, public IPv4 address that can be associated with an EC2 instance.","To provide a private IP address for instances within a subnet.","To assign multiple IP addresses to a single network interface."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the purpose of an Elastic IP address. It is a static, public IPv4 address designed for dynamic cloud computing. You can associate it with an EC2 instance, network interface, or load balancer, and it remains associated with your account until you release it, providing a fixed public endpoint. Option A (incorrect) describes the behavior of a regular public IP address assigned to an EC2 instance, which changes upon restart. Option C (incorrect) describes a private IP address, which is automatically assigned to instances within a subnet. Option D (incorrect) describes the functionality of an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) or secondary private IP addresses, not an Elastic IP address itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_42',
  'A SysOps Administrator is setting up a highly available connection between an on-premises data center and an Amazon VPC over the public internet. Which AWS service should be used to establish this secure and encrypted connection?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Direct Connect","VPC Peering","AWS Site-to-Site VPN","VPC Endpoints"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Site-to-Site VPN. This service creates an encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your Amazon VPC over the public internet, making it suitable for secure hybrid connectivity. Option A (incorrect) AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated private connection, not one over the public internet. Option B (incorrect) VPC Peering connects two VPCs within AWS, not an on-premises data center. Option D (incorrect) VPC Endpoints provide private access to AWS services from within a VPC, not connectivity to on-premises networks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_43',
  'What is the primary purpose of AWS Transit Gateway?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide private access to AWS services from a VPC.","To enable direct, dedicated network connections to AWS from on-premises.","To connect multiple VPCs and on-premises networks through a central hub.","To allow instances in a private subnet to access the internet."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the primary purpose of AWS Transit Gateway. It acts as a network transit hub, simplifying the connection of multiple Amazon VPCs and on-premises networks into a single, managed gateway. Option A (incorrect) describes VPC Endpoints (AWS PrivateLink). Option B (incorrect) describes AWS Direct Connect. Option D (incorrect) describes a NAT Gateway.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_44',
  'Which AWS service is used to create and manage virtual networks (VPCs) in the AWS Cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","Amazon S3","Amazon VPC","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon VPC (Virtual Private Cloud). It allows you to provision a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define. Option A (incorrect) Amazon EC2 provides virtual servers (instances) but not the virtual network itself. Option B (incorrect) Amazon S3 is an object storage service. Option D (incorrect) AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_45',
  'What is the purpose of a subnet in an Amazon VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["To define a virtual private network connection to an on-premises data center.","To logically divide a VPC into smaller network segments.","To control inbound and outbound traffic for EC2 instances.","To provide a dedicated connection for AWS services within the VPC."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the purpose of a subnet. A subnet is a range of IP addresses in your VPC. You can launch AWS resources, such as EC2 instances, into a subnet. Subnets allow you to segment your network for security, performance, or operational reasons. Option A (incorrect) defines a VPN or Direct Connect connection. Option C (incorrect) describes the function of security groups or NACLs. Option D (incorrect) describes VPC Endpoints.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_46',
  'Which AWS service allows you to create a secure, encrypted tunnel over the public internet between your on-premises network and your Amazon VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Direct Connect","AWS Site-to-Site VPN","VPC Peering","AWS Transit Gateway"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Site-to-Site VPN. This service creates an encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your Amazon VPC over the public internet. Option A (incorrect) AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated private connection, not one over the public internet. Option C (incorrect) VPC Peering connects two VPCs within AWS, not an on-premises network. Option D (incorrect) AWS Transit Gateway acts as a central hub for connecting VPCs and on-premises networks, but it still relies on VPN or Direct Connect for the actual on-premises connection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_47',
  'Which AWS service allows you to create a logically isolated virtual network within the AWS Cloud?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","Amazon S3","Amazon VPC","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon VPC (Virtual Private Cloud). Amazon VPC enables you to provision a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define. Option A (incorrect) Amazon EC2 provides virtual servers, but not the network itself. Option B (incorrect) Amazon S3 is an object storage service. Option D (incorrect) AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_48',
  'What is the primary purpose of an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) in Amazon EC2?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a static public IP address for an instance.","To enable an instance to connect to the internet.","To attach multiple network interfaces to an instance, allowing for multi-IP configurations.","To provide a dedicated connection between an instance and an AWS service."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the primary purpose of an Elastic Network Interface (ENI). An ENI is a virtual network interface that you can attach to an instance in your VPC. It can include a primary private IPv4 address, one or more secondary private IPv4 addresses, one Elastic IP address, and one or more security groups, enabling complex networking configurations and multi-IP setups. Option A (incorrect) describes an Elastic IP address. Option B (incorrect) describes the function of an Internet Gateway and a public IP address. Option D (incorrect) describes a VPC Endpoint.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_49',
  'Which AWS service enables you to establish a dedicated, private network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS, bypassing the public internet?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Site-to-Site VPN","VPC Peering","AWS Direct Connect","AWS Transit Gateway"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Direct Connect. This service provides a dedicated network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS, offering a consistent and high-bandwidth private connection that does not traverse the public internet. Option A (incorrect) AWS Site-to-Site VPN creates an encrypted connection over the public internet. Option B (incorrect) VPC Peering connects two VPCs within AWS. Option D (incorrect) AWS Transit Gateway acts as a central hub for connecting VPCs and on-premises networks, but it still relies on Direct Connect or VPN for the actual on-premises connection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_50',
  'A company has an application deployed in a private subnet within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC). The application needs to download software updates from the internet but must not be directly accessible from the internet. The operations team requires a highly available and fully managed solution for outbound internet access. Which AWS service should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["Deploy an Amazon EC2 instance with a public IP address and configure it as a NAT instance.","Attach an Internet Gateway to the private subnet''s route table.","Provision an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection to an on-premises NAT device.","Deploy an Amazon VPC NAT Gateway in a public subnet and configure private subnet route tables."]'::json,
  '{3}'::int[],
  'Option D (correct) is the recommended solution. An Amazon VPC NAT Gateway provides a highly available and fully managed service for instances in a private subnet to connect to the internet or other AWS services, while preventing the internet from initiating connections to those instances. It is deployed in a public subnet, and private subnets are configured to route internet-bound traffic through it. Option A (incorrect) is a valid but less preferred solution. A NAT instance requires manual setup, patching, scaling, and high availability configuration, incurring significant operational overhead compared to a managed NAT Gateway. Option B (incorrect) would allow inbound internet access to the private subnet, which violates the requirement that the application must not be directly accessible from the internet. An Internet Gateway is for public subnets. Option C (incorrect) is for connecting an on-premises network to a VPC, not for providing outbound internet access from a private subnet within the VPC itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_51',
  'A security-conscious organization needs to ensure that Amazon EC2 instances in a private subnet can access Amazon S3 buckets for storing application logs without routing traffic through the public internet. They want to minimize the attack surface and maintain strict network isolation. Which type of VPC endpoint should be configured?',
  'mcq',
  '["An Interface VPC Endpoint for Amazon S3.","A Gateway VPC Endpoint for Amazon S3.","An AWS Direct Connect connection to Amazon S3.","A VPC peering connection to another VPC with S3 access."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the appropriate choice for privately accessing Amazon S3. A Gateway VPC Endpoint provides private connectivity from your VPC to Amazon S3 (and DynamoDB) without requiring an Internet Gateway, NAT device, VPN connection, or AWS Direct Connect connection. It''s a gateway that you specify as a target in your route table. Option A (incorrect) is for services that support AWS PrivateLink, which creates an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) in your subnet. While S3 now supports Interface Endpoints for specific API operations, the Gateway Endpoint is the traditional and often simpler solution for general S3 access from a VPC and is more aligned with the ''Gateway'' concept for S3. Option C (incorrect) establishes a dedicated network connection from an on-premises data center to AWS, which is not relevant for private access from within a VPC to S3. Option D (incorrect) connects two VPCs, but S3 is a global service, not typically accessed via another VPC''s S3 access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_52',
  'A large enterprise has deployed multiple applications across 10 different Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) in the same AWS Region. They need to establish full mesh connectivity between all these VPCs while minimizing the number of network connections and simplifying routing management. Which AWS networking service is the most scalable and operationally efficient solution?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure VPC peering connections between all 10 VPCs.","Use an AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection from each VPC to a central VPN concentrator.","Deploy an AWS Transit Gateway and attach all VPCs to it.","Create an Elastic Load Balancer in each VPC and use cross-VPC routing."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the most scalable and operationally efficient solution for connecting multiple VPCs in a hub-and-spoke model. AWS Transit Gateway acts as a central hub, simplifying network architecture and reducing the number of connections needed. For 10 VPCs, it requires only 10 attachments to the Transit Gateway. Option A (incorrect) is a common anti-pattern (ap-5.1-001). VPC peering is non-transitive and requires N*(N-1)/2 connections for full mesh connectivity. For 10 VPCs, this would mean 10*(9)/2 = 45 peering connections, which is unmanageable and not scalable. Option B (incorrect) would introduce significant operational overhead by requiring the management of a central VPN concentrator (likely an EC2 instance) and numerous VPN connections, which is not a fully managed AWS service for inter-VPC connectivity. Option D (incorrect) is for distributing incoming application traffic across targets, not for providing general inter-VPC network connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_53',
  'A company needs to securely connect its on-premises data center to its Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) in AWS over the public internet. The connection must be encrypted and provide reliable communication for data transfer. Which AWS service should be used to establish this hybrid connectivity?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Direct Connect.","VPC peering.","AWS Site-to-Site VPN.","An Internet Gateway with security groups."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the appropriate service for this scenario. An AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection establishes a secure, encrypted tunnel over the public internet between your on-premises network and your AWS VPC. It is a cost-effective solution for secure hybrid connectivity when a dedicated private connection is not required. Option A (incorrect) provides a dedicated private network connection, which offers higher bandwidth and lower latency but is more expensive and not over the public internet. Option B (incorrect) is used to connect two VPCs within AWS, not an on-premises data center to a VPC. Option D (incorrect) provides internet access to a VPC but does not establish a secure, encrypted tunnel for private communication with an on-premises data center.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_54',
  'A financial institution requires a dedicated, high-bandwidth, and low-latency network connection between its on-premises data center and its AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC). The connection must bypass the public internet to meet strict security and performance compliance requirements. Which AWS service should be utilized?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Site-to-Site VPN.","AWS Direct Connect.","VPC peering.","An Internet Gateway with a highly secure VPN appliance."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the ideal service for this requirement. AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated, private network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS. This bypasses the public internet, offering consistent network performance, reduced bandwidth costs, and enhanced security, which is crucial for financial institutions. Option A (incorrect) establishes an encrypted connection over the public internet, which does not meet the requirement for bypassing the public internet or the high-bandwidth, low-latency demands of a dedicated connection. Option C (incorrect) is used to connect two VPCs within AWS, not an on-premises data center to a VPC. Option D (incorrect) still relies on the public internet and does not provide the dedicated, private connection required for strict security and performance compliance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_55',
  'An architect is designing a three-tier web application in an AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC). The application consists of public-facing web servers, internal application servers, and a database. The web servers must be accessible from the internet, while the application servers and database must remain private and inaccessible from the internet. How should the subnets be configured to meet these security and accessibility requirements?',
  'mcq',
  '["Place all three tiers in a single public subnet with strict security group rules.","Place all three tiers in a single private subnet and use a NAT Gateway for internet access.","Place web servers in public subnets and application/database servers in private subnets.","Place web servers in private subnets and application/database servers in public subnets."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the standard and most secure architectural pattern for a multi-tier application in a VPC. Public subnets are associated with an Internet Gateway and contain resources that need to be directly accessible from the internet (like web servers). Private subnets do not have a direct route to an Internet Gateway and contain resources that should not be publicly accessible (like application servers and databases), typically accessing the internet via a NAT Gateway if outbound access is needed. Option A (incorrect) is a security anti-pattern as it exposes all tiers to the internet, relying solely on security groups, which is less secure than network-level isolation. Option B (incorrect) would make the web servers inaccessible from the internet, failing the requirement for public accessibility. Option D (incorrect) reverses the security posture, exposing the application and database servers to the internet while hiding the web servers, which is an insecure configuration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_56',
  'A company needs to host a web server on an Amazon EC2 instance that must have a consistent public IP address, even if the instance is stopped and started or replaced. This static IP is required for external services to reliably connect to the web server. Which AWS networking feature should be used to meet this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Assign a public IP address to the EC2 instance during launch.","Use a Network Load Balancer in front of the EC2 instance.","Associate an Elastic IP address with the EC2 instance.","Configure an Internet Gateway and attach it to the EC2 instance."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the solution for a static public IP address. An Elastic IP address is a static, public IPv4 address designed for dynamic cloud computing. You can associate an Elastic IP address with an EC2 instance, and it remains associated even if the instance is stopped, started, or replaced, ensuring a consistent public endpoint. Option A (incorrect) provides a public IP address, but this IP address changes every time the instance is stopped and started, or terminated and replaced, which does not meet the requirement for a consistent IP. Option B (incorrect) provides a static IP for the load balancer itself, but it''s a load balancer, not directly for a single EC2 instance, and might be overkill if only a single instance needs a static IP. Option D (incorrect) is necessary for internet connectivity for instances in a public subnet but does not provide a static public IP address for a specific instance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_57',
  'An organization needs to assign multiple private IP addresses to a single Amazon EC2 instance for a network appliance that acts as a firewall. These additional IP addresses must be able to be moved between instances for high availability purposes. Which AWS networking component allows for this configuration?',
  'mcq',
  '["An Elastic IP address.","A secondary private IP address on the primary Elastic Network Interface (ENI).","A new VPC peering connection.","An Internet Gateway."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the appropriate solution. An Elastic Network Interface (ENI) can have multiple private IP addresses. You can assign secondary private IP addresses to an existing ENI. These secondary IP addresses can be moved between ENIs (and thus between EC2 instances) within the same subnet, which is useful for implementing high availability for network appliances. Option A (incorrect) provides a static public IP address, not multiple private IP addresses for an instance. Option C (incorrect) is for connecting two VPCs, not for assigning multiple IP addresses to a single instance. Option D (incorrect) is for enabling internet connectivity for a VPC and is not related to assigning multiple private IPs to an instance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_58',
  'An application running on Amazon EC2 instances in a private subnet needs to connect to an external API over the internet. The private subnet''s route table must be configured to direct all outbound internet-bound traffic through a NAT Gateway. Which entry should be added to the private subnet''s route table?',
  'mcq',
  '["A route with destination `0.0.0.0/0` and target as the Internet Gateway.","A route with destination `0.0.0.0/0` and target as the NAT Gateway ID.","A route with destination `10.0.0.0/16` and target as the NAT Gateway ID.","A route with destination `0.0.0.0/0` and target as the local VPC CIDR."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the correct entry. To route all outbound internet-bound traffic from a private subnet through a NAT Gateway, you must add a route to the private subnet''s route table with a destination of `0.0.0.0/0` (representing all IP addresses outside the VPC) and a target of the NAT Gateway ID. Option A (incorrect) would route traffic directly to an Internet Gateway, which is only appropriate for public subnets and would bypass the NAT Gateway, potentially exposing private instances. Option C (incorrect) specifies a local VPC CIDR block as the destination, which is incorrect for internet-bound traffic. Option D (incorrect) would create a loop or misdirect traffic as `0.0.0.0/0` should point outside the VPC, not back to the local VPC CIDR.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_59',
  'A software vendor wants to offer their SaaS application as a service to customers running their own Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) in AWS. The customers need to access the vendor''s application privately, without exposing it to the public internet or requiring complex VPC peering configurations. Which AWS service enables this private, secure, and simplified service consumption?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Site-to-Site VPN.","AWS Direct Connect.","AWS PrivateLink.","VPC peering."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is specifically designed for this use case. AWS PrivateLink allows consumers to access services hosted in another VPC (or by other AWS accounts or third parties) privately, using an Interface VPC Endpoint. This eliminates the need for an Internet Gateway, NAT device, VPN connection, or VPC peering, simplifying network architecture and enhancing security by keeping traffic within the AWS network. Option A (incorrect) is for connecting on-premises networks to AWS over the internet, not for private service consumption between VPCs. Option B (incorrect) is for dedicated private connections from on-premises to AWS, not for inter-VPC service access. Option D (incorrect) can connect two VPCs but becomes complex and unscalable for many customers, and it doesn''t provide the same level of service abstraction as PrivateLink.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_60',
  'What is the primary purpose of an AWS Transit Gateway?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a managed relational database service.","To connect thousands of Amazon VPCs and on-premises networks through a central hub.","To store and retrieve objects at scale.","To run serverless compute functions."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) describes the primary purpose of an AWS Transit Gateway. It simplifies network topology by acting as a central hub for connecting multiple VPCs and on-premises networks, eliminating the need for complex peering relationships. Option A refers to Amazon RDS. Option C refers to Amazon S3. Option D refers to AWS Lambda.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_61',
  'Which AWS service provides a dedicated network connection from your on-premises data center to AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Site-to-Site VPN","Amazon VPC","AWS Direct Connect","AWS Transit Gateway"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Direct Connect. It establishes a dedicated private network connection between your data center, office, or colocation environment and AWS, offering consistent network performance and reduced bandwidth costs compared to internet-based connections. Option A (AWS Site-to-Site VPN) provides a secure, encrypted connection over the public internet. Option B (Amazon VPC) is the fundamental building block for your virtual network in AWS. Option D (AWS Transit Gateway) is used for connecting multiple VPCs and on-premises networks, but not for providing the dedicated physical connection itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_62',
  'What is the main function of a NAT Gateway within a VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["To allow instances in a public subnet to communicate with the internet.","To allow instances in a private subnet to initiate outbound connections to the internet while preventing inbound connections.","To distribute incoming application traffic across multiple targets, such as EC2 instances.","To provide private connectivity to AWS services from within a VPC."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the main function of a NAT Gateway. It enables instances in a private subnet to connect to the internet or other AWS services outside the VPC, but prevents external hosts from initiating connections to those instances. Option A describes the function of an Internet Gateway. Option C describes an Elastic Load Balancer. Option D describes VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_63',
  'What is an Elastic IP address primarily used for in Amazon EC2?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a dynamic public IP address that changes upon instance restart.","To ensure that an instance always has a static public IPv4 address, even if the instance is stopped and started.","To assign multiple private IP addresses to a single network interface.","To encrypt data in transit between EC2 instances."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the primary use of an Elastic IP address. It is a static, public IPv4 address that you can allocate to your AWS account and associate with an EC2 instance, network interface, or Elastic Load Balancer. This ensures that the public IP address remains constant, even if the underlying instance is stopped and started. Option A describes a regular public IP address that is automatically assigned and changes upon restart. Option C describes secondary private IP addresses on an ENI. Option D describes network encryption, which is handled by other services or protocols.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_64',
  'What is the primary use case for AWS Site-to-Site VPN?',
  'mcq',
  '["To connect multiple AWS VPCs within the same AWS account.","To establish a secure and encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your AWS VPC over the public internet.","To provide high-speed, dedicated network connectivity between AWS Regions.","To enable private access to AWS services from instances in a private subnet."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the primary use case for AWS Site-to-Site VPN. It creates an encrypted tunnel over the public internet, allowing secure communication between your on-premises network and your AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC). Option A is typically handled by VPC peering or AWS Transit Gateway. Option C is more aligned with AWS Direct Connect or inter-region VPC peering. Option D is handled by VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_65',
  'What is the purpose of a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) in AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide a global content delivery network for static and dynamic web content.","To allow you to provision a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.","To offer fully managed object storage for any type of data.","To enable serverless execution of code in response to events."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes the purpose of an Amazon VPC. It gives you complete control over your virtual networking environment, including selection of your own IP address range, creation of subnets, and configuration of route tables and network gateways. Option A describes Amazon CloudFront. Option C describes Amazon S3. Option D describes AWS Lambda.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_66',
  'What is the function of an Internet Gateway in a VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["To allow instances in a private subnet to access the internet.","To enable communication between instances in different subnets within the same VPC.","To provide a connection between a VPC and the public internet, allowing instances in public subnets to communicate with the internet.","To establish a private connection to AWS services from within a VPC."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the function of an Internet Gateway. It''s a horizontally scaled, redundant, and highly available VPC component that allows communication between instances in your VPC and the internet. It enables public subnets to send and receive internet traffic. Option A describes a NAT Gateway. Option B describes route tables and local routing. Option D describes VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_67',
  'What is the primary benefit of using an Interface VPC endpoint (powered by AWS PrivateLink)?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows instances in public subnets to communicate with the internet.","It enables private connectivity to AWS services and services hosted by other AWS customers or partners, without requiring an Internet Gateway, NAT device, VPN, or Direct Connect.","It provides a dedicated network connection from an on-premises data center to AWS.","It simplifies network routing for connecting many VPCs together in a hub-and-spoke model."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the primary benefit of an Interface VPC endpoint. It uses AWS PrivateLink to establish a private connection between your VPC and supported AWS services, or even services hosted by other AWS accounts, keeping traffic within the Amazon network. Option A describes an Internet Gateway. Option C describes AWS Direct Connect. Option D describes AWS Transit Gateway.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_1_68',
  'A company has 10 VPCs in the same AWS Region and needs to establish full mesh connectivity between all of them for internal application communication, minimizing operational overhead. Which networking service should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC peering connections between each pair of VPCs.","AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections for each VPC.","An AWS Transit Gateway configured with all VPCs attached.","An Internet Gateway attached to each VPC with public routing."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the most suitable solution. An AWS Transit Gateway provides a scalable hub-and-spoke model for connecting many VPCs and on-premises networks, significantly reducing operational overhead compared to managing numerous individual connections. Option A (VPC peering connections) would require N*(N-1)/2 connections, which for 10 VPCs is 10*(9)/2 = 45 peering connections, leading to high operational overhead and representing anti-pattern ap-5.1-001. Option B (AWS Site-to-Site VPN) is for connecting on-premises networks to VPCs, not for inter-VPC connectivity within AWS. Option D (Internet Gateway with public routing) would expose internal traffic to the public internet, which is insecure and not the intended use for internal application communication.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- Module: m_26_3
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_36',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to analyze network traffic flowing to and from network interfaces in an Amazon VPC to identify potential security issues or connectivity problems. Which AWS service should be enabled for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch Logs","VPC Flow Logs","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is VPC Flow Logs. VPC Flow Logs capture information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC. Flow log data can be published to Amazon CloudWatch Logs or Amazon S3, enabling detailed analysis of network traffic. Option A (incorrect) Amazon CloudWatch Logs is a destination for logs, but VPC Flow Logs is the service that generates the network traffic logs. Option C (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail records API calls and related events made in your AWS account, focusing on actions taken, not network traffic. Option D (incorrect) AWS Config assesses, audits, and evaluates the configurations of your AWS resources, not network traffic itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_37',
  'A SysOps Administrator is troubleshooting an unreachable Amazon EC2 instance within a VPC. The instance has the correct security group rules, but still cannot be accessed. Which AWS service can help analyze the network path between a source and destination to identify potential connectivity issues?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Flow Logs","AWS Reachability Analyzer","Amazon CloudWatch Metrics","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Reachability Analyzer. This tool helps you diagnose network reachability issues between two resources in your VPCs. It performs a static analysis of network configurations to determine if a path exists and identifies blocking components like security groups, NACLs, or route tables. Option A (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs provide historical traffic data but do not perform a real-time path analysis. Option C (incorrect) Amazon CloudWatch Metrics provide performance data but not a detailed network path analysis. Option D (incorrect) AWS Config tracks resource configuration changes and compliance, not live network connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_38',
  'When troubleshooting network connectivity to an EC2 instance, a SysOps Administrator observes that inbound traffic is allowed by the security group, but responses are not returning. What is a key difference between Network ACLs (NACLs) and Security Groups that might explain this behavior?',
  'mcq',
  '["Security groups are stateless, while NACLs are stateful.","NACLs are stateful, while security groups are stateless.","Security groups apply to subnets, while NACLs apply to instances.","NACLs are stateless and require explicit rules for both inbound and outbound traffic."]'::json,
  '{3}'::int[],
  'Option D (correct) highlights the critical difference and represents anti-pattern ap-5.3-001. NACLs are stateless, meaning they do not track the state of connections and require explicit rules for both inbound and outbound traffic, including ephemeral ports for response traffic. If outbound rules are missing, responses will be blocked. Security groups, conversely, are stateful; if you allow inbound traffic, the outbound response traffic is automatically allowed. Option A (incorrect) and Option B (incorrect) incorrectly swap the stateful/stateless properties. Option C (incorrect) incorrectly states that security groups apply to subnets and NACLs apply to instances; it''s the opposite: security groups apply to instances, and NACLs apply to subnets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_39',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to troubleshoot intermittent 5xx errors from an application behind an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB). Which ELB feature can provide detailed information about client requests and the responses sent by the load balancer and its registered targets?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Flow Logs","ELB Access Logs","Amazon CloudWatch Metrics","AWS CloudTrail"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is ELB Access Logs. These logs capture detailed information about requests sent to your load balancer, including the time the request was received, the client''s IP address, latencies, request paths, and server responses. This data is invaluable for troubleshooting application issues and analyzing traffic patterns. Option A (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs capture IP traffic information at the network interface level, which is too low-level for application-specific HTTP/HTTPS request details from an ELB. Option C (incorrect) Amazon CloudWatch Metrics provide aggregated performance data (e.g., HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count) but not individual request details. Option D (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail logs API calls made to AWS services, not application-level requests handled by an ELB.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_40',
  'What is the primary purpose of connection draining on an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)?',
  'mcq',
  '["To redirect traffic to a different region during a disaster.","To ensure that in-flight requests are completed before deregistering instances.","To prevent new connections from being established to unhealthy instances.","To distribute incoming traffic evenly across all registered instances."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the primary purpose of connection draining. When an instance is deregistered or becomes unhealthy, connection draining ensures that the load balancer stops sending new requests to the instance but keeps existing connections open for a configurable duration to allow in-flight requests to complete gracefully. Option A (incorrect) redirecting traffic to a different region is typically handled by Route 53 or Global Accelerator, not connection draining. Option C (incorrect) preventing new connections to unhealthy instances is handled by ELB health checks. Option D (incorrect) distributing incoming traffic evenly is the basic function of a load balancer, not specific to connection draining.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_41',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to monitor the number of network packets received by an Amazon EC2 instance. Which AWS service would provide this metric?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Flow Logs","AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon CloudWatch. CloudWatch collects and processes raw data from AWS services into readable, near real-time metrics. Metrics like ''NetworkPacketsIn'' and ''NetworkPacketsOut'' are available for EC2 instances. Option A (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs capture IP traffic records but do not provide real-time metrics for individual instances. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail records API calls and events, not network performance metrics. Option D (incorrect) AWS Config assesses and audits resource configurations, not operational metrics.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_42',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to troubleshoot why an EC2 instance in a public subnet cannot access the internet, even though it has a public IP address. Which VPC component should be checked first to ensure proper routing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Network Access Control List (NACL)","Security Group","Route Table associated with the subnet","VPC Endpoint"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the Route Table associated with the subnet. For an instance in a public subnet to access the internet, its subnet''s route table must have a default route (0.0.0.0/0) pointing to an Internet Gateway. Without this, traffic cannot leave the VPC to reach the internet. Option A (incorrect) NACLs control traffic at the subnet level, but a missing route is a more fundamental issue for internet access. Option B (incorrect) Security Groups control traffic at the instance level, but again, a missing route prevents traffic from even reaching the security group for outbound internet access. Option D (incorrect) VPC Endpoints provide private access to AWS services, not general internet access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_43',
  'Which AWS service can be used to perform a static analysis of your network configurations to determine if a path exists between two resources in your VPCs and identify any blocking components?',
  'mcq',
  '["VPC Flow Logs","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Reachability Analyzer","Amazon CloudWatch"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Reachability Analyzer. This service performs a static analysis of your network configurations to determine reachability between a source and destination resource, identifying potential blocking components like security groups, NACLs, or route tables. Option A (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs capture actual network traffic, but don''t perform a static path analysis. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail logs API calls, not network path analysis. Option D (incorrect) Amazon CloudWatch monitors metrics and logs, but doesn''t offer a direct network path analysis tool.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_44',
  'A SysOps Administrator is troubleshooting an EC2 instance that cannot receive inbound connections, even though its security group allows the traffic. Which VPC component should be checked next, considering it acts as a stateless firewall for subnets?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Route 53 hosted zone","VPC Flow Logs","Network Access Control List (NACL)","AWS Reachability Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is the Network Access Control List (NACL). NACLs operate at the subnet level and are stateless, meaning they evaluate both inbound and outbound rules independently. If the NACL associated with the instance''s subnet does not explicitly allow the inbound traffic, it will be blocked, even if the security group allows it. Option A (incorrect) Route 53 is for DNS resolution. Option B (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs record traffic but don''t actively block it. Option D (incorrect) AWS Reachability Analyzer helps diagnose, but checking the NACL directly is a primary troubleshooting step.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_45',
  'What is the primary difference between a Security Group and a Network Access Control List (NACL) in an Amazon VPC?',
  'mcq',
  '["Security Groups are stateless; NACLs are stateful.","Security Groups operate at the subnet level; NACLs operate at the instance level.","Security Groups are stateful; NACLs are stateless.","Security Groups only allow inbound rules; NACLs only allow outbound rules."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) states the primary difference. Security Groups are stateful, meaning that if you allow an inbound connection, the outbound response is automatically allowed, and vice-versa. They operate at the instance level. NACLs are stateless, requiring explicit rules for both inbound and outbound traffic, and they operate at the subnet level. Option A (incorrect) incorrectly swaps the stateful/stateless properties. Option B (incorrect) incorrectly swaps the operational levels. Option D (incorrect) is false; both can have inbound and outbound rules.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_26_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_26_m_26_3_46',
  'A SysOps Administrator is troubleshooting an EC2 instance that cannot reach an internal database instance in a different subnet within the same VPC. Both instances'' security groups allow the necessary traffic. What is the next critical VPC component to verify?',
  'mcq',
  '["The Internet Gateway attached to the VPC.","The Route Tables associated with both subnets.","The NAT Gateway in the VPC.","The Amazon Route 53 public hosted zone."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the Route Tables associated with both subnets. For instances in different subnets within the same VPC to communicate, the route tables for both subnets must have explicit routes that direct traffic to the other subnet. If a route is missing or incorrect, traffic will not be able to traverse between the subnets. Option A (incorrect) the Internet Gateway is for internet access, not internal VPC communication. Option C (incorrect) the NAT Gateway is for private subnets to access the internet, not for internal VPC communication. Option D (incorrect) the Amazon Route 53 public hosted zone is for public DNS resolution, not for internal VPC routing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain26_5',
  NOW(),
