  'Option A (correct) is Amazon S3 Standard-Infrequent Access (S3 Standard-IA). This storage class is ideal for data that is accessed less frequently but requires rapid access when needed. It offers lower storage costs than S3 Standard but charges a retrieval fee. Option B (Amazon S3 Standard) is for frequently accessed data. Option C (Amazon S3 Glacier) and Option D (Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive) are for archiving data with longer retrieval times and even lower storage costs.',
