  '["gp3","io2","sc1","st1"]'::json,
  '{3}'::int[],
  'Option D (st1) is the correct EBS volume type. st1 (Throughput Optimized HDD) volumes are designed for frequently accessed, throughput-intensive workloads with large, sequential I/O, such as big data, data warehouses, and log processing. Option A (gp3) is a general-purpose SSD for a wide variety of transactional workloads. Option B (io2) is a provisioned IOPS SSD for I/O-intensive, critical applications. Option C (sc1) is a Cold HDD volume, suitable for less frequently accessed workloads and offers the lowest cost per GB.',
