  'Option C (sc1) is the correct EBS volume type. sc1 (Cold HDD) volumes are designed for the lowest cost per GB for infrequently accessed workloads, where data is accessed less frequently and performance is not a primary concern. Option A (gp3) is a general-purpose SSD. Option B (io2) is a provisioned IOPS SSD for high-performance applications. Option D (st1) is a throughput-optimized HDD for frequently accessed, throughput-intensive workloads.',
