  'q_27_m_27_2_72',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to migrate an existing Amazon EBS gp2 volume to a more cost-effective solution while maintaining or improving performance. Which EBS volume type is the recommended choice?',
  'mcq',
  '["io2","st1","gp3","sc1"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (gp3) is the recommended choice. gp3 volumes offer a baseline of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s at a lower cost than gp2, and their IOPS and throughput can be independently provisioned. Migrating from gp2 to gp3 typically reduces costs by 20% while often improving performance, addressing the anti-pattern (ap-6.2-001) of using gp2 without considering gp3. Option A (io2) is a higher-performance, higher-cost option for I/O-intensive workloads, not primarily a cost-optimization move from gp2. Option B (st1) and Option D (sc1) are HDD-backed volumes, unsuitable for replacing general-purpose SSD gp2 volumes due to their different performance characteristics.',
