VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_75',
  'What is the primary benefit of using Enhanced Networking on Amazon EC2 instances?',
  'mcq',
  '["It provides dedicated physical servers for increased security.","It offers higher bandwidth, higher packet per second (PPS) performance, and lower inter-instance latency.","It enables automatic scaling of instances based on demand.","It encrypts all network traffic between instances by default."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (It offers higher bandwidth, higher packet per second (PPS) performance, and lower inter-instance latency.) correctly describes the primary benefit of Enhanced Networking. Enhanced Networking uses single root I/O virtualization (SR-IOV) to provide high-performance networking capabilities, which is crucial for demanding network-bound applications. Option A describes Dedicated Hosts. Option C describes Auto Scaling. Option D is incorrect; while AWS provides encryption options, Enhanced Networking''s primary benefit is performance.',
