INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_77',
  'A research team requires ultra-low latency and high throughput networking for tightly coupled High-Performance Computing (HPC) workloads running on Amazon EC2. Which networking interface and placement group combination should be utilized?',
  'mcq',
  '["Elastic Network Interface (ENI) with Spread Placement Group","Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) with Cluster Placement Group","Elastic Network Interface (ENI) with Partition Placement Group","Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) with Spread Placement Group"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) with Cluster Placement Group) is the optimal combination for ultra-low latency and high throughput HPC workloads. Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA) is a network device that enables customers to run HPC applications requiring high levels of inter-node communication at scale on AWS. A Cluster Placement Group packs instances close together within an Availability Zone to achieve the lowest possible network latency and highest throughput. Option A and C use ENI, which provides enhanced networking but not the specialized HPC capabilities of EFA. Spread and Partition Placement Groups are designed for fault tolerance and spreading instances, not for ultra-low latency between tightly coupled instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_78',
  'What is the primary function of Amazon RDS Read Replicas?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide automated backups and point-in-time recovery for a database.","To enhance database availability by synchronously replicating data to a standby instance in a different Availability Zone.","To offload read-heavy database traffic from the primary instance and improve read performance.","To cache frequently accessed query results in memory to speed up application responses."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (To offload read-heavy database traffic from the primary instance and improve read performance.) correctly describes the primary function of Amazon RDS Read Replicas. Read Replicas allow you to scale out your database''s read capacity by creating copies that handle read requests, thereby reducing the load on the primary database instance and improving the performance of read-intensive applications. Option A describes automated backups. Option B describes Multi-AZ deployments. Option D describes Amazon ElastiCache.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_79',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to provision a new Amazon EBS volume for a database workload that requires a consistent baseline performance of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s throughput, with the ability to independently scale IOPS and throughput. Cost optimization is also a key consideration. Which EBS volume type offers this independent scalability and a superior cost-performance ratio compared to its predecessor?',
  'mcq',
  '["gp2","io1","gp3","st1"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is gp3. gp3 volumes provide a baseline performance of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s throughput at a lower cost than gp2, and critically, allow you to independently provision IOPS and throughput without increasing the volume size. This offers superior cost-performance for many workloads. Option A (gp2) is an older generation general purpose SSD that links IOPS and throughput to volume size, making it less cost-effective for specific performance needs. Option B (io1) is a Provisioned IOPS SSD designed for mission-critical applications requiring sustained high IOPS, but it is more expensive than gp3. Option D (st1) is a Throughput Optimized HDD designed for frequently accessed, throughput-intensive workloads like big data processing, not for high IOPS databases.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_80',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to improve the read performance and scalability of an Amazon RDS for MySQL database that experiences heavy read traffic from an analytics application. The application can tolerate slightly stale data. Which RDS feature should be implemented to offload read queries from the primary database instance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Multi-AZ deployment","Storage Auto Scaling","Read Replicas","Performance Insights"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon RDS Read Replicas. Read Replicas provide an independent endpoint for read operations, allowing you to offload read traffic from your primary database instance and improve the performance and scalability of read-heavy applications. They are eventually consistent. Option A (Multi-AZ deployment) is for high availability and disaster recovery, not for scaling read performance. Option B (Storage Auto Scaling) automatically increases storage capacity when needed, but it doesn''t address read performance. Option D (Performance Insights) is a database performance monitoring tool, not a scaling solution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_81',
  'For an HPC (High Performance Computing) application that requires extremely low latency and high network throughput between EC2 instances within a single Availability Zone, which EC2 placement group strategy should a SysOps Administrator use?',
  'mcq',
  '["Spread Placement Group","Partition Placement Group","Cluster Placement Group","Dedicated Hosts"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is a Cluster Placement Group. A Cluster Placement Group packs instances close together inside an Availability Zone, enabling low-latency network performance necessary for High Performance Computing (HPC) applications. Option A (Spread Placement Group) places instances on distinct underlying hardware to reduce correlated failures, which is for high availability, not low latency. Option B (Partition Placement Group) divides instances into logical segments called partitions, ensuring instances in different partitions do not share underlying hardware, which is for large distributed workloads, not ultra-low latency. Option D (Dedicated Hosts) provides physical servers for your exclusive use, but doesn''t inherently guarantee the same low-latency network performance between instances as a Cluster Placement Group.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_82',
  'A company hosts a popular public website with users distributed globally. The website serves static content (images, CSS, JavaScript) and dynamic API responses. To improve user experience by reducing content load times and to decrease the load on their origin servers, which AWS service should be used to cache and deliver content closer to the users?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon S3","Amazon CloudFront","AWS Global Accelerator","Amazon Route 53"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon CloudFront. CloudFront is a content delivery network (CDN) that caches content at edge locations around the world, reducing latency for global users and offloading requests from origin servers. It is ideal for delivering both static and dynamic content. Option A (Amazon S3) is an object storage service that can act as an origin for CloudFront but doesn''t provide global caching on its own. Option C (AWS Global Accelerator) improves application availability and performance by directing user traffic to optimal endpoints over the AWS global network, but it focuses on network path optimization rather than content caching. Option D (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service and does not cache content.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_83',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to provision an Amazon EBS volume for a critical transactional database that requires extremely high IOPS and consistent, low-latency performance. The workload is sensitive to any performance degradation. Which EBS volume type is specifically designed for the highest performance and mission-critical applications?',
  'mcq',
  '["gp3","st1","io2","sc1"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is io2. io2 (Provisioned IOPS SSD) volumes are designed for mission-critical, high-performance applications that require sustained IOPS performance and low latency. They offer the highest durability and are suitable for large transactional databases. Option A (gp3) is a general-purpose SSD with good performance and cost-effectiveness but not the highest IOPS. Option B (st1) is a Throughput Optimized HDD for large, sequential workloads. Option D (sc1) is a Cold HDD for infrequently accessed data, offering the lowest cost per GB but with very low performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_84',
  'A company runs a high-traffic e-commerce website where product catalog data is frequently accessed from an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. To reduce the load on the database and improve response times for read-heavy operations, a SysOps Administrator wants to implement an in-memory caching layer for this product data. Which combination of AWS services would best achieve this performance optimization?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon RDS with Multi-AZ","Amazon RDS with Read Replicas","Amazon ElastiCache with Amazon RDS","Amazon DynamoDB with DAX"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon ElastiCache with Amazon RDS. Amazon ElastiCache provides a fully managed, in-memory caching service (supporting Redis or Memcached) that can significantly improve application performance by caching frequently accessed data, thereby reducing the load on the Amazon RDS database and speeding up data retrieval. Option A (Amazon RDS with Multi-AZ) provides high availability and disaster recovery, not read scaling or caching. Option B (Amazon RDS with Read Replicas) improves read scalability by offloading read queries to separate instances, but it''s still a database, not an in-memory cache for ultra-low latency access. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB with DAX) is a caching solution for DynamoDB, which is a NoSQL database, not a relational database like PostgreSQL.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_85',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to deploy several critical EC2 instances for an application where each instance must be isolated on distinct underlying hardware to minimize correlated failures. This is crucial for maintaining high availability. Which EC2 placement group strategy should be used to ensure instances are on separate physical servers?',
  'mcq',
  '["Cluster Placement Group","Spread Placement Group","Partition Placement Group","Dedicated Instances"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is a Spread Placement Group. A Spread Placement Group ensures that instances are launched on distinct underlying hardware, reducing the risk of correlated failures that could occur if multiple instances were to share the same physical server. This is ideal for applications requiring high availability with a small number of critical instances. Option A (Cluster Placement Group) packs instances close together for low network latency, which increases the risk of correlated failures. Option C (Partition Placement Group) divides instances into logical segments across racks, suitable for large distributed workloads, but not for ensuring distinct hardware for a small number of critical instances. Option D (Dedicated Instances) ensures instances run on hardware dedicated to a single customer but does not guarantee distinct underlying hardware for individual instances within that customer''s account.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_86',
  'To improve network performance for Amazon EC2 instances by reducing latency and increasing packet per second (PPS) performance, a SysOps Administrator can enable a specific feature. Which feature provides significantly higher network performance for supported instance types?',
  'mcq',
  '["EC2 Auto Scaling","Enhanced Networking","Placement Groups","Elastic Load Balancing"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Enhanced Networking. Enhanced Networking uses single root I/O virtualization (SR-IOV) to provide high-performance networking capabilities on supported EC2 instance types. It delivers significantly higher packet per second (PPS) performance, lower inter-instance latency, and lower network jitter. Option A (EC2 Auto Scaling) automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances in response to demand. Option C (Placement Groups) influence the placement of instances for specific network or availability requirements but don''t inherently provide enhanced networking capabilities. Option D (Elastic Load Balancing) distributes incoming application traffic across multiple targets, such as EC2 instances, but doesn''t directly enhance the networking performance of individual instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_87',
  'A research institution is running a tightly coupled High Performance Computing (HPC) application on Amazon EC2 that requires very low latency and high bandwidth networking between instances. This application frequently performs inter-node communication. Which specialized networking interface is designed to provide the highest level of inter-instance communication performance for HPC and machine learning workloads?',
  'mcq',
  '["Elastic Network Interface (ENI)","Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA)","Enhanced Networking","AWS Direct Connect"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Elastic Fabric Adapter (EFA). EFA is a network interface for Amazon EC2 instances that enables customers to run HPC and machine learning applications requiring high levels of inter-node communication at scale on AWS. EFA uses a custom-built operating system bypass technique to provide lower and more consistent latency and higher throughput than traditional TCP networking. Option A (Elastic Network Interface - ENI) is a basic virtual network interface for EC2. Option C (Enhanced Networking) provides higher PPS and lower latency than standard networking but EFA goes further for HPC. Option D (AWS Direct Connect) establishes a dedicated network connection from your premises to AWS, which is for hybrid cloud connectivity, not inter-instance communication within AWS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_88',
  'Which Amazon EBS volume type is a General Purpose SSD that balances price and performance for a wide variety of transactional workloads, offering a baseline performance of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s throughput, with independently configurable IOPS and throughput?',
  'mcq',
  '["gp2","io1","gp3","sc1"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is gp3. gp3 is the latest generation General Purpose SSD volume type that provides a baseline of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s throughput, with the ability to independently provision additional IOPS and throughput without increasing the volume size. It offers a superior cost-performance ratio compared to gp2. Option A (gp2) is the previous generation General Purpose SSD where IOPS and throughput scale with volume size. Option B (io1) is a Provisioned IOPS SSD for mission-critical applications requiring sustained high IOPS. Option D (sc1) is a Cold HDD for infrequently accessed data, offering the lowest cost per GB but with very low performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_89',
  'A popular online news portal uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL database as its backend. During peak news events, the website experiences a surge in read traffic, leading to performance bottlenecks on the primary database instance. The content served can be slightly delayed (eventually consistent). Which RDS feature should the SysOps Administrator implement to handle the increased read load and improve database responsiveness?',
  'mcq',
  '["Multi-AZ deployment","Read Replicas","Performance Insights","Storage Auto Scaling"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon RDS Read Replicas. Read Replicas allow you to create one or more copies of your primary database instance, which can then serve read traffic. This offloads read queries from the primary instance, improving its performance and allowing the application to scale read operations horizontally, which is ideal for read-heavy workloads like a news portal. Option A (Multi-AZ deployment) is for high availability and disaster recovery, not for scaling read performance. Option C (Performance Insights) is a monitoring tool to analyze database performance, not a scaling solution. Option D (Storage Auto Scaling) automatically increases storage capacity but does not address CPU or I/O bottlenecks caused by high read loads.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_90',
  'A SysOps Administrator is evaluating Amazon EBS volume types for a new application. The application requires a balance of price and performance for a wide range of transactional workloads, such as development and test environments, and boot volumes. Which EBS volume type is a cost-effective General Purpose SSD suitable for these balanced workloads?',
  'mcq',
  '["io2","st1","gp3","sc1"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) is gp3. gp3 volumes are General Purpose SSDs that offer a balance of price and performance for a wide variety of transactional workloads, including boot volumes, development and test environments, and low-latency interactive applications. They provide a baseline of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s throughput, with independent scalability. Option A (io2) is a Provisioned IOPS SSD for the most demanding, mission-critical applications. Option B (st1) is a Throughput Optimized HDD for large, sequential workloads. Option D (sc1) is a Cold HDD for infrequently accessed data, offering the lowest cost but with very low performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_91',
  'A company needs to deliver large video files and software updates to a global user base. They want to ensure fast download speeds and reduce the load on their origin S3 bucket. Which AWS service should the SysOps Administrator configure to cache and distribute these large files efficiently worldwide?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration","Amazon CloudFront","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon Route 53"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon CloudFront. CloudFront is a content delivery network (CDN) that caches content at edge locations around the world, significantly reducing latency and improving download speeds for global users. It also reduces the load on the origin server, such as an S3 bucket. Option A (Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration) speeds up long-distance data transfers to and from S3 buckets, but it''s primarily for uploads/downloads to the bucket itself, not for global content distribution and caching. Option C (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated network connection from your premises to AWS, which is not for public content distribution. Option D (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service and does not cache or distribute content.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_27_m_27_2_92',
  'A SysOps Administrator is setting up a new Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database for a critical application. To ensure high availability and automatic failover in case of an Availability Zone outage, which deployment option should be chosen?',
  'mcq',
  '["Single-AZ deployment","Multi-AZ deployment","Read Replicas","Aurora Serverless"]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is Multi-AZ deployment. An Amazon RDS Multi-AZ deployment provisions and maintains a synchronous standby replica in a different Availability Zone. In case of an outage of the primary instance or its Availability Zone, RDS automatically fails over to the standby replica, ensuring high availability and data durability. Option A (Single-AZ deployment) does not provide automatic failover to another AZ. Option C (Read Replicas) are for scaling read performance and are eventually consistent, not primarily for high availability with synchronous replication. Option D (Aurora Serverless) is a serverless option for Amazon Aurora, which scales compute capacity automatically, but Multi-AZ is the specific feature for high availability across AZs for standard RDS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain27_5',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_27_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

