  'Which of the following are benefits of using AWS Config for resource management and compliance? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Real-time application performance monitoring","Continuous monitoring of resource configurations","Automated remediation of non-compliant resources","Interactive querying of log data","Recording of all API calls made in an account"]'::json,
  '{1,2}'::int[],
  'Option B (Continuous monitoring of resource configurations) is a primary function of AWS Config, which tracks changes to your AWS resource configurations over time. Option C (Automated remediation of non-compliant resources) is also a key capability, allowing AWS Config to trigger AWS Systems Manager Automation documents or AWS Lambda functions to automatically bring non-compliant resources back into compliance. Option A (Real-time application performance monitoring) is typically handled by services like Amazon CloudWatch Application Insights or custom CloudWatch metrics. Option D (Interactive querying of log data) is provided by CloudWatch Logs Insights. Option E (Recording of all API calls made in an account) is the function of AWS CloudTrail.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_22_m_22_1_58',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to ensure that Amazon EC2 instances are monitored for memory and disk space utilization. Which actions are required to collect these metrics? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Enable default Amazon CloudWatch metrics for EC2","Install and configure the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances","Configure AWS CloudTrail to log EC2 events","Create custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch","Enable EC2 instance status checks"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Install and configure the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances) is necessary because default Amazon CloudWatch metrics for EC2 instances do not include memory or disk space utilization (anti-pattern ap-1.1-001). The agent collects these OS-level metrics. Option D (Create custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch) is the mechanism through which the CloudWatch Agent sends the collected memory and disk space data to CloudWatch. Option A (Enable default Amazon CloudWatch metrics for EC2) is insufficient as it only provides CPU utilization, network I/O, and disk I/O. Option C (Configure AWS CloudTrail to log EC2 events) records API calls, not performance metrics. Option E (Enable EC2 instance status checks) monitors the health of the instance and underlying hypervisor, but not specific OS-level resource usage like memory or disk space.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
