  'Option B (correct) and Option C (correct) are key characteristics of Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Users can define custom metrics to monitor application-specific data, and all metrics are organized into namespaces to prevent naming conflicts. Option A is incorrect; raw log events are stored in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Option D describes CloudWatch Logs retention policies. Option E is incorrect because while CloudWatch automatically collects metrics from many AWS services, the CloudWatch agent allows collecting custom metrics from EC2 instances and on-premises servers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_22_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

