  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'To automatically recover from underlying hardware failures, Option B (correct) should be configured. EC2 Auto Recovery automatically restarts an instance on new hardware when a system status check fails, preserving its configuration. Option D (correct) is crucial because Auto Recovery is triggered by a failed System status check, indicating an issue with the underlying host. Option A is insufficient as Instance status checks monitor the OS, not the host hardware. Option C involves manual recovery or automation that doesn''t preserve instance ID/EIP in the same way as Auto Recovery. Option E is for notification, not automatic recovery.',
