  'Option C (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service that allows you to run code in response to events, which is central to serverless automation. Option D (Amazon EventBridge) can capture events from various AWS services and route them to targets like AWS Lambda functions, enabling event-driven automation. Option A (AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager) is for OS patching. Option B (AWS CodeDeploy) is for application deployment. Option E (AWS OpsWorks) is a configuration management service that typically involves managing servers.',
