  'To configure EC2 Auto Recovery, you begin by creating an Amazon CloudWatch alarm specifically for the ''StatusCheckFailed_System'' metric, which indicates underlying host issues (Option A). Within the alarm configuration, you must specify the particular EC2 instance that the alarm should monitor (Option B). Next, you define the threshold and evaluation period for the alarm, determining when it should trigger (Option C). Finally, as the alarm action, you select ''Recover'' to automatically restart the instance on a new healthy host while preserving its ID and other metadata (Option D).',
