  'To automate a response to an operational event using Amazon EventBridge, the first step is to prepare the action to be taken. Option D (Create an AWS Lambda function to perform the desired action) ensures that the automated task is ready. Next, Option A (Define the event pattern for the desired operational event (e.g., EC2 instance state change)) specifies which events EventBridge should listen for. After defining the event pattern, Option C (Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with the defined event pattern) establishes the rule that detects these events. Finally, Option B (Configure the Lambda function as a target for the EventBridge rule) links the detected event to the Lambda function, enabling the automated response.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain22_5',
  NOW(),
  43,
