  'Option C (Identify the correct EBS snapshot) is the first logical step to ensure the correct data is restored. Option B (Create a new EBS volume from the snapshot) must follow, as a volume is created from a snapshot. Option A (Attach the new EBS volume to an EC2 instance) is necessary to make the volume accessible to a compute resource. Finally, Option D (Verify data integrity on the attached volume) is a critical post-restoration step to confirm the process was successful and the data is usable.',
