INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_79',
  'A company needs to implement a disaster recovery strategy for its critical data stored in Amazon S3, aiming for low RPO and RTO. Order the steps to configure S3 Cross-Region Replication.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable S3 Versioning on the source bucket","Configure Cross-Region Replication (CRR) rules on the source bucket","Create a destination S3 bucket in a different AWS Region","Ensure appropriate IAM permissions for replication"]'::json,
  '{0,2,3,1}'::int[],
  'To implement S3 Cross-Region Replication for disaster recovery, the first prerequisite is to enable S3 Versioning on the source bucket (Option A), as CRR requires versioning to be active. Next, a destination S3 bucket must be created in the desired target AWS Region (Option C). Before configuring the replication rules, it''s crucial to ensure that the necessary IAM permissions are in place for S3 to replicate objects between buckets (Option D). Finally, you configure the Cross-Region Replication rules on the source bucket, specifying the destination and any filters (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_80',
  'A development team needs to ensure that their Amazon EBS volumes are regularly backed up and can be easily restored to a previous state. Order the steps to implement an automated snapshot strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (DLM) policy","Define the snapshot schedule and retention rules","Associate the DLM policy with target EBS volumes","Monitor snapshot creation and deletion"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'To implement an automated snapshot strategy for Amazon EBS volumes, the first step is to create an Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (DLM) policy (Option A). Within this policy, you define the specific snapshot schedule and retention rules (Option B), such as how often snapshots are taken and for how long they are kept. Next, you associate this DLM policy with the target EBS volumes (Option C), typically using tags. Finally, it''s crucial to monitor the snapshot creation and deletion processes (Option D) to ensure the policy is working as intended and meeting backup requirements.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_81',
  'A company is planning to migrate an on-premises application to AWS and needs to define its Recovery Time Objective (RTO) and Recovery Point Objective (RPO). Order the general steps to determine these objectives.',
  'ordering',
  '["Identify critical business functions and their impact of downtime","Determine the maximum acceptable data loss (RPO)","Determine the maximum acceptable downtime (RTO)","Select appropriate AWS backup and DR strategies"]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}'::int[],
  'To determine RTO and RPO, the foundational step is to identify critical business functions and understand the impact of their downtime (Option A). This analysis helps in prioritizing. Based on this, you then determine the maximum acceptable downtime, which defines the Recovery Time Objective (RTO) (Option C). Concurrently, you determine the maximum acceptable data loss, which defines the Recovery Point Objective (RPO) (Option B). Once RTO and RPO are established, you can select appropriate AWS backup and disaster recovery strategies that meet these defined objectives (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_82',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to configure Amazon RDS automated backups for a new database instance. Order the steps to ensure backups are enabled and properly retained.',
  'ordering',
  '["Specify the backup retention period","Enable automated backups during instance creation","Monitor backup status and available restore points","Define the backup window"]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}'::int[],
  'To configure Amazon RDS automated backups, the first step is to enable automated backups when creating or modifying the RDS instance (Option B). During this process, you specify the backup retention period (Option A), which determines how long backups are kept for point-in-time recovery. You also define the backup window (Option D), which is the preferred time for automated backups to occur. Finally, after configuration, it''s essential to monitor the backup status and available restore points (Option C) to ensure the backups are being taken successfully and are available for recovery.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_83',
  'A media company manages a critical Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database that stores user metadata and content catalog information. The company requires a robust backup and restore strategy to meet an RPO of 5 minutes and an RTO of 30 minutes, ensuring business continuity in case of data corruption or accidental deletion. The operations team needs to implement and validate a point-in-time recovery process for this database. Order the following steps to achieve this objective, ensuring the solution is fully tested and compliant with the RPO/RTO requirements.',
  'ordering',
  '["Initiate a point-in-time restore operation to a new Amazon RDS instance, specifying a timestamp within the retention period.","Enable automated backups for the Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL instance with a retention period exceeding the RPO objective.","Validate the restored data on the new Amazon RDS instance to confirm integrity and completeness against the RPO.","Monitor the automated backup process to ensure successful snapshot creation and log archiving."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}'::int[],
  'To ensure point-in-time recovery (PITR) for an Amazon RDS database, the first step is to enable and configure automated backups. Option B (Enable automated backups for the Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL instance with a retention period exceeding the RPO objective) is the foundational step, as PITR relies on these automated backups and transaction logs. Following this, Option D (Monitor the automated backup process to ensure successful snapshot creation and log archiving) is crucial to confirm that backups are consistently being taken, which directly impacts the ability to meet the RPO. Option A (Initiate a point-in-time restore operation to a new Amazon RDS instance, specifying a timestamp within the retention period) is the next logical step, performing an actual restore to test the process. Finally, Option C (Validate the restored data on the new Amazon RDS instance to confirm integrity and completeness against the RPO) is essential to verify that the restore was successful and that the recovered data meets the RPO, directly addressing the anti-pattern of not testing restore procedures (ap-2.3-001).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_84',
  'A large enterprise needs to centralize its backup operations for various AWS services, including Amazon EC2 instances, Amazon EBS volumes, and Amazon RDS databases, to meet stringent compliance requirements and reduce operational overhead. The goal is to define consistent backup policies, manage retention, and ensure recoverability across these diverse resources. Order the following steps to implement a centralized backup strategy using AWS Backup.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a backup plan within AWS Backup, specifying backup frequency, retention periods, and lifecycle rules.","Assign the EC2 instances, EBS volumes, and RDS databases to the created backup plan.","Create a backup vault in AWS Backup to store the encrypted backups.","Test the restore process for each service type to validate the RTO and RPO objectives."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}'::int[],
  'To centralize backups with AWS Backup, a vault is required first. Option C (Create a backup vault in AWS Backup to store the encrypted backups) is the initial step, as it provides the secure storage location for all backups. Next, Option A (Define a backup plan within AWS Backup, specifying backup frequency, retention periods, and lifecycle rules) outlines the policies for how backups should be taken and managed. Option B (Assign the EC2 instances, EBS volumes, and RDS databases to the created backup plan) then links the target resources to these defined policies. Finally, Option D (Test the restore process for each service type to validate the RTO and RPO objectives) is a critical step to ensure the backup strategy is effective and meets recovery requirements, directly addressing the anti-pattern of not testing restore procedures (ap-2.3-001).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_85',
  'A global analytics company uses Amazon DynamoDB for its high-performance, low-latency data storage for real-time dashboards. To ensure business continuity and meet an RPO of seconds, the company needs to implement a robust backup and restore mechanism that allows for point-in-time recovery. The solution must be easy to manage and automatically protect against accidental table modifications or deletions. Order the following steps to configure and validate this DynamoDB data protection strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Perform a point-in-time restore operation on the DynamoDB table to a new table, specifying a recovery timestamp.","Enable Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR) for the Amazon DynamoDB table.","Verify the integrity and completeness of the data in the newly restored DynamoDB table.","Monitor the DynamoDB table''s activity to ensure PITR is actively capturing changes."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}'::int[],
  'For DynamoDB point-in-time recovery, enablement is the first step. Option B (Enable Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR) for the Amazon DynamoDB table) is the initial and essential action to begin continuous backups. Following enablement, Option D (Monitor the DynamoDB table''s activity to ensure PITR is actively capturing changes) is crucial to confirm that the service is functioning as expected and capturing all modifications. Option A (Perform a point-in-time restore operation on the DynamoDB table to a new table, specifying a recovery timestamp) is the next logical step to test the recovery process. Finally, Option C (Verify the integrity and completeness of the data in the newly restored DynamoDB table) is critical to validate that the restore was successful and that the data meets the RPO, addressing the anti-pattern of not testing restore procedures (ap-2.3-001).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_86',
  'A financial services company needs to establish a comprehensive disaster recovery plan for its core trading application, which consists of multiple Amazon EC2 instances and an Amazon RDS database. The goal is to achieve an RPO of 15 minutes and an RTO of 1 hour, using a warm standby strategy in a separate AWS Region. The operations team must ensure that the entire application stack can be recovered and validated efficiently. Order the following steps to implement and validate this warm standby DR strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Provision a cross-Region read replica for the Amazon RDS database in the secondary AWS Region and ensure it is synchronized.","Configure Amazon Route 53 to use a failover routing policy with health checks pointing to the primary Region''s application endpoint.","Deploy a minimal, scaled-down version of the EC2 application stack in the secondary AWS Region, configured to connect to the read replica.","Perform a full DR test by initiating a failover to the secondary Region and validating application functionality and data integrity."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}'::int[],
  'A warm standby DR strategy requires both data and a minimal application stack to be ready in the secondary region. Option A (Provision a cross-Region read replica for the Amazon RDS database in the secondary AWS Region and ensure it is synchronized) is the first critical step for data replication, ensuring a low RPO. Next, Option C (Deploy a minimal, scaled-down version of the EC2 application stack in the secondary AWS Region, configured to connect to the read replica) establishes the ''warm standby'' infrastructure. Option B (Configure Amazon Route 53 to use a failover routing policy with health checks pointing to the primary Region''s application endpoint) sets up the DNS for the primary region, which will be updated during failover. Finally, Option D (Perform a full DR test by initiating a failover to the secondary Region and validating application functionality and data integrity) is essential to validate the entire DR process and confirm RTO/RPO, directly addressing the anti-pattern of not testing restore procedures (ap-2.3-001).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

