INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_69',
  'A web application needs to be highly available across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) using an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling. Order the steps to configure this architecture.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and target groups","Configure an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a launch template","Ensure the launch template specifies instances across multiple AZs","Attach the Auto Scaling group to the ALB target group"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'To build a highly available web application with ALB and EC2 Auto Scaling, the first step is to create an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and its associated target groups (Option A), which will distribute incoming traffic. Next, configure an EC2 Auto Scaling group (Option B), which manages the fleet of EC2 instances. Within the Auto Scaling group configuration, ensure the launch template specifies that instances should be launched across multiple Availability Zones (Option C) for high availability. Finally, attach the Auto Scaling group to the ALB target group (Option D) so that the ALB can route traffic to the instances managed by the Auto Scaling group.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_70',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to ensure an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database is highly available. Order the steps to enable Multi-AZ deployment for an existing RDS instance.',
  'ordering',
  '["Modify the existing RDS instance to enable Multi-AZ","Monitor the Multi-AZ conversion process","Verify the instance status shows ''Multi-AZ: Yes''","Test failover by rebooting with failover"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'To enable Multi-AZ for an existing Amazon RDS instance, the first step is to modify the instance and select the Multi-AZ option (Option A). After initiating the modification, it''s important to monitor the Multi-AZ conversion process (Option B), which involves creating a standby replica. Once the conversion is complete, verify that the instance status in the RDS console shows ''Multi-AZ: Yes'' (Option C). Finally, to confirm the high availability setup, it''s a best practice to test failover by rebooting the instance with failover (Option D), which simulates a primary instance failure and ensures the standby takes over.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_71',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to provide shared storage for multiple Amazon EC2 instances within the same VPC across different Availability Zones. Order the steps to set up Amazon EFS for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon EFS file system","Create mount targets in each desired Availability Zone","Mount the EFS file system on EC2 instances","Configure security groups to allow NFS traffic"]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}'::int[],
  'To set up Amazon EFS for shared storage across multiple EC2 instances, the first step is to create an Amazon EFS file system (Option A). After creating the file system, you must create mount targets (Option B) in each Availability Zone where your EC2 instances reside, allowing them to access the file system. Before mounting, it''s crucial to configure security groups (Option D) associated with the EFS mount targets and the EC2 instances to allow NFS (port 2049) traffic. Finally, you can mount the EFS file system on your EC2 instances (Option C) using the mount helper or standard NFS client.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_72',
  'A company is deploying a new application and wants to ensure its database tier, running on Amazon RDS, is highly available. Order the steps to configure a Multi-AZ deployment for a new RDS instance.',
  'ordering',
  '["Select the desired database engine and instance class","Enable the Multi-AZ deployment option","Configure network and security settings (VPC, subnets, security groups)","Launch the RDS instance and monitor its creation"]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}'::int[],
  'When configuring a new Amazon RDS instance for Multi-AZ deployment, the initial step is to select the desired database engine and instance class (Option A). Next, you configure the network and security settings, including the VPC, subnets (ensuring they span multiple AZs), and security groups (Option C). Crucially, you then enable the Multi-AZ deployment option (Option B) during the instance configuration. Finally, you launch the RDS instance and monitor its creation process (Option D) to ensure it provisions correctly with the Multi-AZ standby replica.',
