  '{0,2,1,3}'::int[],
  'To deploy EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones using an Auto Scaling group, the first step is to create a launch template (Option A) that defines the EC2 instance configuration (AMI, instance type, security groups, etc.). Next, create an Auto Scaling group (Option C) and crucially specify the multiple Availability Zones where instances should be launched. Then, define the desired capacity and scaling policies (Option B) for the Auto Scaling group to manage the number of instances. Finally, verify that instances are successfully launched and distributed across the specified AZs (Option D) to confirm high availability.',
