INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_75',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to configure Route 53 health checks for an application running on an EC2 instance. Order the steps to create and associate a basic health check.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a Route 53 health check","Specify the endpoint to monitor (e.g., IP address or domain)","Associate the health check with a Route 53 DNS record","Define the health check parameters (e.g., protocol, port, interval)"]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}'::int[],
  'To configure a Route 53 health check, the initial step is to create a Route 53 health check (Option A) within the Route 53 console. Then, you must specify the endpoint to monitor (Option B), which could be an IP address, a domain name, or an endpoint in another AWS service. Next, you define the health check parameters (Option D), such as the protocol (HTTP, TCP), port, and evaluation interval. Finally, to make the health check effective, you associate it with a Route 53 DNS record (Option C), allowing Route 53 to update DNS based on the endpoint''s health.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_76',
  'A company wants to ensure its Amazon S3 data is resilient against regional outages. Order the steps to configure S3 Cross-Region Replication for a bucket.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable S3 Versioning on the source bucket","Create a destination S3 bucket in a different AWS Region","Configure a replication rule on the source bucket","Grant necessary IAM permissions for S3 replication"]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}'::int[],
  'To configure S3 Cross-Region Replication, the first prerequisite is to enable S3 Versioning on the source bucket (Option A), as CRR relies on versioning. Next, a destination S3 bucket must be created in a different AWS Region (Option B) to serve as the replication target. Before setting up the replication rule, it''s essential to grant the necessary IAM permissions (Option D) to allow S3 to replicate objects. Finally, you configure a replication rule on the source bucket (Option C), specifying the destination bucket and any filters for objects to replicate.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_77',
  'An online gaming platform uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to distribute traffic to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. To ensure players experience minimal latency and continuous gameplay, the ALB must accurately identify and route traffic only to healthy instances. The operations team needs to configure robust health checks for the ALB''s target groups to ensure high availability of the game servers. Order the following steps to properly configure ALB health checks.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a target group for the EC2 instances, specifying the protocol and port for instance registration.","Configure the health check settings within the target group, including protocol, port, path, and success codes.","Register the Amazon EC2 instances (or an Auto Scaling group) with the defined target group.","Monitor the health status of the registered instances in the Amazon EC2 console or CloudWatch metrics."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'Configuring Application Load Balancer health checks begins with defining where traffic should go. Option A (Define a target group for the EC2 instances, specifying the protocol and port for instance registration) is the initial step to group the backend instances. Next, Option B (Configure the health check settings within the target group, including protocol, port, path, and success codes) specifies how the ALB will determine instance health. Option C (Register the Amazon EC2 instances (or an Auto Scaling group) with the defined target group) links the actual compute resources to the target group. Finally, Option D (Monitor the health status of the registered instances in the Amazon EC2 console or CloudWatch metrics) is crucial for ongoing operational visibility and troubleshooting, ensuring the health checks are working as intended.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_78',
  'A real-time bidding application requires a high-performance, low-latency caching layer to reduce database load and improve response times. The caching solution must be highly available and fault-tolerant, capable of surviving an Availability Zone outage. The operations team decides to implement a Multi-AZ Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster. Order the following steps to deploy this highly available caching solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster, enabling Multi-AZ with automatic failover and selecting the appropriate node type.","Create a subnet group for ElastiCache that spans at least two Availability Zones within the VPC.","Configure the application to connect to the ElastiCache cluster endpoint and implement caching logic.","Ensure the security group associated with the ElastiCache cluster allows inbound traffic from the application''s EC2 instances."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}'::int[],
  'Deploying a Multi-AZ Amazon ElastiCache cluster requires a subnet group spanning multiple AZs. Option B (Create a subnet group for ElastiCache that spans at least two Availability Zones within the VPC) is the prerequisite for Multi-AZ deployment. Next, Option A (Create an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster, enabling Multi-AZ with automatic failover and selecting the appropriate node type) provisions the actual cache cluster with high availability features. Option D (Ensure the security group associated with the ElastiCache cluster allows inbound traffic from the application''s EC2 instances) is a critical networking step to allow the application to connect to the cache. Finally, Option C (Configure the application to connect to the ElastiCache cluster endpoint and implement caching logic) integrates the application with the newly deployed cache.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_79',
  'A global media company operates a content delivery platform with users distributed worldwide. To optimize user experience and minimize latency, the company wants to route user requests to the closest available server endpoint. The platform uses Amazon EC2 instances in multiple AWS Regions. The operations team needs to configure Amazon Route 53 to achieve latency-based routing for its primary domain. Order the following steps to implement this routing policy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a resource record set for the primary domain in Route 53, pointing to the EC2 endpoint in `us-east-1` with a Latency routing policy.","Create a resource record set for the primary domain in Route 53, pointing to the EC2 endpoint in `eu-west-1` with a Latency routing policy.","Ensure that the EC2 instances in each AWS Region are running and accessible via their respective public IP addresses or Elastic IP addresses.","Verify that Route 53 correctly resolves the domain to the lowest latency endpoint from various geographical locations."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}'::int[],
  'Implementing Route 53 Latency-based routing requires having accessible endpoints in different regions. Option C (Ensure that the EC2 instances in each AWS Region are running and accessible via their respective public IP addresses or Elastic IP addresses) is the foundational step, as there must be endpoints for Route 53 to route to. Next, Option A (Create a resource record set for the primary domain in Route 53, pointing to the EC2 endpoint in `us-east-1` with a Latency routing policy) defines one of the regional endpoints. Option B (Create a resource record set for the primary domain in Route 53, pointing to the EC2 endpoint in `eu-west-1` with a Latency routing policy) defines another regional endpoint. Route 53 automatically evaluates latency to determine the best endpoint. Finally, Option D (Verify that Route 53 correctly resolves the domain to the lowest latency endpoint from various geographical locations) is crucial to confirm the routing policy is functioning as intended and delivering the desired user experience.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_2_80',
  'A SysOps Administrator is setting up Amazon Route 53 to provide DNS failover for a web application hosted on Amazon EC2 instances across two Availability Zones. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to configure a basic failover routing policy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a primary record set pointing to the healthy endpoint in the preferred Availability Zone.","Create a health check that monitors the health of the application endpoint.","Associate the health check with the primary and secondary record sets.","Create a secondary record set with a lower priority pointing to the endpoint in the backup Availability Zone."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}'::int[],
  'For Amazon Route 53 DNS failover, monitoring the endpoint''s health is critical. Option B (Create a health check) must be the first step, as it defines the criteria for determining endpoint availability. Option A (Create a primary record set) is next, as this record will point to the active resource and rely on the health check. Option D (Create a secondary record set) follows, providing the failover target, also relying on a health check. Finally, Option C (Associate the health check) links the health check to both the primary and secondary record sets, enabling Route 53 to automatically switch traffic based on the health status. Failing to associate health checks would mean the failover routing policy would not detect failures, which is an anti-pattern.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_23_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

