  'To configure an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a target tracking scaling policy, the first step is to create the EC2 Auto Scaling group itself, referencing a launch template that defines the instance configuration (Option A). Next, you define a target tracking scaling policy (Option B), which is the recommended method for dynamic scaling. Within this policy, you specify the target metric (e.g., Average CPU Utilization) and the desired target value (Option C) that the Auto Scaling group should maintain. Finally, it''s crucial to monitor the Auto Scaling group''s scaling activities (Option D) to ensure it''s responding correctly to changes in demand.',
