  'To create and configure an Amazon RDS Read Replica, the initial step is to select the source Amazon RDS DB instance (Option A) from which the replica will be created. Next, you initiate the creation of a Read Replica from this source instance (Option B), specifying its configuration. Once the Read Replica is provisioned and synchronized, you must update application connection strings (Option C) to direct read traffic to the Read Replica''s endpoint. Finally, it''s important to continuously monitor replication lag and performance (Option D) to ensure the Read Replica is serving its purpose effectively and staying up-to-date with the primary instance.',
