  'To enable storage auto-scaling for an existing Amazon RDS instance, the first step is to modify the existing Amazon RDS instance (Option A) through the AWS Management Console or API. Within the modification options, you then enable the ''Storage autoscaling'' option (Option B). Crucially, you must specify the maximum storage threshold (Option C) to set an upper limit on how much storage RDS can provision. Finally, it''s a best practice to monitor storage utilization metrics (Option D) to observe the auto-scaling in action and ensure it meets the database''s needs without exceeding the defined maximum.',
