  'To configure DynamoDB Auto Scaling, the initial step is to select the specific DynamoDB table (Option A) for which you want to enable auto-scaling. Next, you enable DynamoDB Auto Scaling (Option B) for the table. Within the auto-scaling configuration, you define the target utilization (Option C) for both read and write capacity units (RCUs and WCUs), which tells DynamoDB the desired percentage of provisioned capacity to use. Finally, it''s essential to monitor the table''s provisioned and consumed capacity (Option D) through Amazon CloudWatch to observe how auto-scaling adjusts capacity in response to traffic.',
