  '{0,2,1,3}'::int[],
  'To create an EC2 Auto Scaling group, the first step is to create a launch template (Option A). This template specifies the Amazon Machine Image (AMI), instance type, security groups, and other configuration details for the instances. Next, you create an Auto Scaling group (Option C), which references this launch template. Then, you define the desired capacity (minimum, maximum, and desired instances) and scaling policies (Option B) for the group. Finally, it''s important to monitor instance health and scaling events (Option D) to ensure the Auto Scaling group is functioning as expected.',
