  'To enable DynamoDB on-demand capacity mode, the first step is to select the specific DynamoDB table (Option A) you wish to modify. Next, you change the table''s capacity mode to ''On-demand'' (Option B) through the AWS Management Console or API. After the change is initiated, you should verify the capacity mode change in the table details (Option C) to confirm it has been applied successfully. Finally, it''s crucial to monitor the table''s performance and costs (Option D) to ensure the on-demand mode is meeting performance requirements while managing expenses effectively, as pricing differs from provisioned capacity.',
