VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_1_72',
  'A SysOps Administrator needs to ensure an application running on Amazon EC2 instances can handle sudden spikes in traffic. Order the steps to configure an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a simple scaling policy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an EC2 Auto Scaling group","Define a CloudWatch alarm for a specific metric (e.g., CPU Utilization)","Create a simple scaling policy to add/remove instances","Associate the CloudWatch alarm with the scaling policy"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'To configure an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a simple scaling policy, the first step is to create the EC2 Auto Scaling group itself (Option A), defining its launch template and desired capacity. Next, you define a CloudWatch alarm (Option B) for a specific metric, such as CPU Utilization, that will trigger scaling actions. Then, you create a simple scaling policy (Option C) within the Auto Scaling group to specify how many instances to add or remove when the alarm state changes. Finally, you associate the CloudWatch alarm with this simple scaling policy (Option D) to link the metric threshold to the scaling action.',
