  '{0,1,3,2}'::int[],
  'To configure DynamoDB Auto Scaling, the first step is to select the specific DynamoDB table in the AWS Management Console (Option A). Then, you navigate to the ''Capacity'' tab for that table and enable Auto Scaling (Option B). Next, you define the target utilization percentage (Option D) for both read and write capacity units, which is the desired metric for Auto Scaling to maintain. Finally, you set the minimum and maximum provisioned capacity units (Option C) to define the boundaries within which Auto Scaling can operate, preventing over-provisioning or under-provisioning beyond acceptable limits.',
