  'To ensure configuration compliance for Amazon EC2 instances using AWS Systems Manager State Manager, the first step is to define a Systems Manager document, which outlines the desired state or configuration actions (Option B). Next, you create an association that links this document to your target EC2 instances, specifying which instances should have this configuration applied (Option A). During association creation, you specify the schedule for how often the configuration should be checked and applied, along with compliance reporting options (Option C). Finally, you verify the compliance status of the target instances in the Systems Manager console to ensure they adhere to the defined state (Option D).',
