  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'Setting up AWS Config involves a logical progression. Option A (Enable the AWS Config recorder) is the foundational step, as Config cannot record anything until it''s enabled. Option B (Select the specific resource types to record) specifies which resources Config should monitor. Option C (Define a custom AWS Config rule or choose a managed rule) is where compliance logic is introduced to evaluate recorded configurations. Option D (Review and confirm the AWS Config settings) is the final confirmation before Config begins its operations.',
