  'To attach an Elastic IP address to an EC2 instance, first allocate a new Elastic IP address in the EC2 console (Option A). Once allocated, select that specific Elastic IP address from the list of available EIPs (Option B). Then, choose ''Actions'' and select the ''Associate Elastic IP address'' option (Option C). Finally, select the target EC2 instance and its private IP address to complete the association (Option D).',
