  'To create a private subnet, you must first have an Amazon VPC (Option A). Within that VPC, you then define an IPv4 CIDR block for the new subnet (Option B). With the CIDR block defined, you can proceed to create the new subnet within the VPC (Option C). The defining characteristic of a private subnet is that its associated route table does not contain a direct route to an Internet Gateway (Option D), preventing direct internet access.',
