  'Before initiating a VPC peering connection, it is critical to ensure that the CIDR blocks of the two VPCs do not overlap (Option D), as overlapping CIDRs prevent peering. Next, create a VPC peering connection request from the requester VPC to the acceptor VPC (Option B). The owner of the acceptor VPC must then accept this peering connection request (Option A). Finally, update the route tables in both VPCs (Option C) to include routes to the peered VPC''s CIDR block, directing traffic through the peering connection.',
