  'To enable private access to Amazon S3, first create a Gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 in the desired VPC (Option A). Next, modify the route tables associated with the subnets where instances need S3 access (Option B) to include a route that directs S3 traffic to the newly created endpoint. Ensure that the security groups and Network ACLs (Option C) attached to the instances and subnets allow outbound traffic to S3. Finally, verify that instances in the specified subnets can access Amazon S3 privately (Option D), confirming the setup.',
