  'To implement a hub-and-spoke topology with AWS Transit Gateway, first, create a Transit Gateway in the desired AWS Region (Option A). Next, create Transit Gateway attachments for each VPC (spoke VPCs) that needs to connect to the hub (Option B). After attachments are established, configure the Transit Gateway route tables (Option C) to define how traffic flows between the attached VPCs, acting as the central routing mechanism. Finally, update the route tables within each attached VPC (Option D) to direct traffic destined for other VPCs through their respective Transit Gateway attachment.',
