  'Cost optimization for EC2 instances typically starts with eliminating waste. Option B (correct) is to identify and terminate idle or underutilized instances. Next, Option C involves right-sizing active instances to match workload demands using tools like AWS Compute Optimizer. After right-sizing, Option D suggests leveraging pricing models like Reserved Instances or Savings Plans for predictable workloads. Finally, Option A emphasizes ongoing monitoring to ensure sustained cost efficiency.',
