  'Optimizing S3 costs for varying access patterns begins with understanding how data is used. Option A (correct) involves analyzing object access patterns. Based on this analysis, Option D suggests enabling S3 Intelligent-Tiering for data where access patterns are unknown or change frequently. For data with predictable access and retention, Option C is to implement S3 Lifecycle policies to transition objects to cheaper storage classes or expire them. Finally, Option B is to regularly review reports to ensure optimizations are effective.',
