  'A development team needs to run fault-tolerant, stateless batch processing jobs on Amazon EC2 instances, aiming for the lowest possible cost. Order the steps to provision these resources using Amazon EC2 Spot Instances.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the Spot Instance interruptions and adjust the application''s tolerance or bidding strategy if necessary.","Define the instance types, Availability Zones, and target capacity for the Spot Fleet request.","Prepare the application to gracefully handle Spot Instance interruptions and checkpoint its progress.","Submit a Spot Fleet request or launch individual Spot Instances with a maximum price."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}'::int[],
  'Before provisioning, Option C (Prepare the application to gracefully handle Spot Instance interruptions and checkpoint its progress) is essential for fault tolerance. Next, Option B (Define the instance types, Availability Zones, and target capacity for the Spot Fleet request) specifies the desired resources. Then, Option D (Submit a Spot Fleet request or launch individual Spot Instances with a maximum price) initiates the provisioning of the instances. Finally, Option A (Monitor the Spot Instance interruptions and adjust the application''s tolerance or bidding strategy if necessary) is an ongoing operational task to ensure job completion and cost efficiency.',
