  'Relying solely on individual alarms for related issues can lead to multiple alarms firing simultaneously, which can cause significant alert noise. Composite alarms combine the states of multiple alarms using logical operators, which helps reduce alert noise by alerting on root causes rather than every symptom. Alert fatigue is a common result of receiving too many alerts, often due to an excessive number of individual alarms without proper aggregation.',
