  '{"A":"RPO of seconds, RTO of minutes","B":"RPO of minutes, RTO of hours","C":"RPO of hours, RTO of days","D":"RPO of zero, RTO of seconds"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'For an RPO of seconds and RTO of minutes (left item 0), a Multi-AZ architecture combined with Cross-Region Replication is often suitable, as it provides rapid failover and near real-time data synchronization. An RPO of minutes and RTO of hours (left item 1) can typically be met with a Pilot Light strategy, where core services are running in a standby region and data is frequently replicated. For an RPO of hours and RTO of days (left item 2), a simple Backup and Restore strategy to another Region is often sufficient, as it involves restoring from backups after an event. An RPO of zero and RTO of seconds (left item 3) requires an Active-Active Multi-Region architecture, where traffic is distributed across multiple regions simultaneously, ensuring continuous operation with no data loss.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  18,
  '{"left":["RPO of seconds, RTO of minutes","RPO of minutes, RTO of hours","RPO of hours, RTO of days","RPO of zero, RTO of seconds"],"right":["Multi-AZ with Cross-Region Replication","Pilot Light with frequent backups","Backup and Restore to another Region","Active-Active Multi-Region"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_105',
  'A large enterprise is implementing a comprehensive backup strategy across its AWS environment. Match the backup type or feature to the AWS service it primarily protects.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Automated Snapshots","B":"Point-in-Time Recovery","C":"Versioning","D":"Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Automated Snapshots (left item 0) are a key feature of Amazon EBS, allowing for incremental backups of volumes. Point-in-Time Recovery (left item 1) is a critical feature for Amazon RDS, enabling restoration of a database to any specified second within a retention period. Versioning (left item 2) is a feature of Amazon S3 that helps protect objects from accidental deletion or overwrites by keeping multiple versions. Cross-Region Snapshot Copy (left item 3) is a capability for Amazon EBS snapshots, allowing them to be copied to different AWS Regions for disaster recovery purposes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  19,
  '{"left":["Automated Snapshots","Point-in-Time Recovery","Versioning","Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"],"right":["Amazon EBS volumes","Amazon RDS databases","Amazon S3 objects","Amazon EBS for DR"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_106',
  'An application relies on a relational database and requires a recovery strategy that minimizes data loss and downtime. Match the RDS backup feature to its specific role in meeting RTO/RPO objectives.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"RDS Automated Backups","B":"RDS Manual Snapshots","C":"RDS Point-in-Time Recovery","D":"RDS Multi-AZ Deployment"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'RDS Automated Backups (left item 0) involve daily full snapshots of your database plus transaction logs, enabling point-in-time recovery. RDS Manual Snapshots (left item 1) are user-initiated backups that can be retained indefinitely, serving as long-term retention points or for specific restore scenarios. RDS Point-in-Time Recovery (left item 2) allows you to restore your database to any specific second within your backup retention period, minimizing data loss (RPO). RDS Multi-AZ Deployment (left item 3) provides synchronous replication of your database to a standby instance in a different Availability Zone, primarily for high availability and automated failover, significantly reducing RTO.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  20,
  '{"left":["RDS Automated Backups","RDS Manual Snapshots","RDS Point-in-Time Recovery","RDS Multi-AZ Deployment"],"right":["Daily full backups plus transaction logs","User-defined, long-term retention points","Restore to any second within retention window","Synchronous replication for high availability"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_107',
  'A company needs to implement a cost-effective backup solution for its EC2 instances and associated EBS volumes. Match the EBS backup strategy to its primary characteristic.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"EBS Snapshots","B":"EBS Lifecycle Manager","C":"EBS Fast Snapshot Restore (FSR)","D":"EBS Multi-Attach"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'EBS Snapshots (left item 0) are incremental backups of your EBS volumes, capturing only the blocks that have changed since the last snapshot, making them cost-effective for long-term retention and point-in-time recovery. EBS Lifecycle Manager (left item 1) automates the creation, retention, and deletion of EBS snapshots and EBS-backed AMIs, simplifying backup management. EBS Fast Snapshot Restore (FSR) (left item 2) enables you to create fully provisioned EBS volumes from snapshots instantly, significantly reducing restore times. EBS Multi-Attach (left item 3) allows you to attach a single Provisioned IOPS SSD (io1 or io2) volume to multiple EC2 instances in the same Availability Zone, which is for shared storage, not directly a backup feature.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  21,
  '{"left":["EBS Snapshots","EBS Lifecycle Manager","EBS Fast Snapshot Restore (FSR)","EBS Multi-Attach"],"right":["Incremental, point-in-time backups","Automates snapshot creation and deletion","Accelerates volume restoration from snapshots","Attaches a single volume to multiple instances"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_108',
  'A development team is designing a highly available application that stores data in Amazon S3. Match the S3 feature to its role in ensuring data durability and resilience.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"S3 Standard storage class","B":"S3 Versioning","C":"S3 Cross-Region Replication","D":"S3 Object Lock"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon S3 Standard storage class (left item 0) is designed for 99.999999999% (11 nines) durability and stores data redundantly across multiple devices in multiple Availability Zones. S3 Versioning (left item 1) keeps multiple versions of an object in the same bucket, protecting against accidental overwrites or deletions. S3 Cross-Region Replication (left item 2) automatically and asynchronously copies objects across S3 buckets in different AWS Regions, providing a robust disaster recovery solution for data. S3 Object Lock (left item 3) prevents objects from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed amount of time or indefinitely, supporting regulatory compliance requirements for data retention.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  22,
  '{"left":["S3 Standard storage class","S3 Versioning","S3 Cross-Region Replication","S3 Object Lock"],"right":["Designed for 99.999999999% durability","Protects against accidental overwrites/deletions","Asynchronously copies objects to another Region","Prevents object deletion for a fixed period"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_23_m_23_3_109',
  'A company needs to implement a robust backup and restore strategy for its critical data across various AWS services. Match the AWS service to its primary backup and recovery mechanism.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon EBS","B":"Amazon RDS","C":"Amazon S3","D":"Amazon DynamoDB"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon EBS (left item 0) uses Snapshots for point-in-time backups of volumes, which are incremental and can be used to restore volumes. Amazon RDS (left item 1) provides Automated Backups and Point-in-Time Recovery, allowing restoration of a database to any second within a retention period. Amazon S3 (left item 2) offers Versioning to protect against accidental overwrites/deletions and Cross-Region Replication for data durability across regions. Amazon DynamoDB (left item 3) provides Point-in-Time Recovery for continuous backups and restoration to any second within the last 35 days.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain23_5',
  NOW(),
  23,
  '{"left":["Amazon EBS","Amazon RDS","Amazon S3","Amazon DynamoDB"],"right":["Snapshots for point-in-time volume recovery","Automated backups and point-in-time recovery","Versioning and Cross-Region Replication for objects","Point-in-Time Recovery for continuous backups"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_23_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

